{"parentUuid":"5458fbaa-e44b-43ab-8ca9-925bc0b59603","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"resp_068d6491e9629980016a7a522679d88191bd676ebf7a0fb998","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"codex-gpt-5-6-sol","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1968,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":237056,"output_tokens":117,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_xuz3b2zG9s2FQdGpVzJFkBk7","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\read-api.ts","offset":1,"limit":65}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_details":null},"attributionSkill":"simplify","type":"assistant","uuid":"62cc7a5f-d5a4-4414-aa79-b33b27b1e67a","timestamp":"2026-08-10T22:35:23.343Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.226","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"62cc7a5f-d5a4-4414-aa79-b33b27b1e67a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0a8de032-5fd3-4106-bcf4-797ed6a2efc2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_xuz3b2zG9s2FQdGpVzJFkBk7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t/**\n2\t * (COMPANION-BRIDGE) — read endpoints: hello, tree, transcript, question,\n3\t * heartbeat (§6.2, §7.2, §7.3, §7.4, §7.7).\n4\t *\n5\t * Reads mutate nothing and are therefore safe to retry. Note the naming\n6\t * inversion this module has to live with: in CODE a *project* is the repo row in\n7\t * the sidebar and a *workspace* is a branch/worktree; the user says these the\n8\t * other way round. The protocol uses the CODE names and the client presents the\n9\t * user's labels.\n10\t *\n11\t * Transcript text is sent VERBATIM. The bridge does not scrub secrets — a\n12\t * partial scrub would be a false assurance. The confidentiality control is the\n13\t * sealed envelope, not filtering.\n14\t *\n15\t * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n16\t * WHAT THIS MODULE REFUSES TO INVENT\n17\t * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n18\t *  - There is no `green` / \"ready for review\" status and there never will be.\n19\t *    The review axis lives in renderer storage the bridge cannot reach.\n20\t *    `needs_input` (red), `working` (yellow) and `idle` (neutral) are the whole\n21\t *    vocabulary; a fourth state synthesised from coarse data would be a lie.\n22\t *  - No status decay ON A LIVE TERMINAL. A binding whose last event was `Start`\n23\t *    three days ago is reported as `working`, because that is what the host\n24\t *    actually recorded. Inventing a timeout would manufacture a state\n25\t *    transition that never happened. (`TerminalAgentStore.clearWorkspaceStatuses`\n26\t *    is the existing escape hatch for a wedged agent, and it runs on the host\n27\t *    side.) This says NOTHING about a terminal that no longer exists — see\n28\t *    `(BRIDGE-LIVENESS)` below, which is not decay but existence.\n29\t *  - No guessed transcript when the agent session is unknown: the read fails\n30\t *    loud rather than serving somebody else's conversation.\n31\t *\n32\t * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n33\t * WHAT THIS MODULE FILTERS, AND IN WHICH DIRECTION IT FAILS\n34\t * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n35\t * Two filters stand between `host.db` and the phone, and they are independent:\n36\t *\n37\t *  - `(BRIDGE-SIDEBAR-FILTER)` — CURATION. The user's sidebar, projected into\n38\t *    `host.db` by `(SIDEBAR-MIRROR)`: soft-deleted, completed, archived,\n39\t *    snoozed and hidden threads are off the desktop's default sidebar and are\n40\t *    therefore off the phone, and a repo the user removed from their sidebar\n41\t *    takes its threads with it.\n42\t *  - `(BRIDGE-LIVENESS)` — EXISTENCE. `status = 'active'` is not liveness; the\n43\t *    daemon's own listing is. 403 rows on this machine matched the old\n44\t *    predicate, 8 of them frozen on `PermissionRequest` and badging the phone\n45\t *    with permanently-blocked agents that had not existed for weeks.\n46\t *\n47\t * BOTH FAIL TOWARD SHOWING. Uncertainty — an unfilled mirror, a workspace with\n48\t * no mirrored row, an unreachable daemon, a stale snapshot — always renders the\n49\t * row. Hiding a real blocked agent is the only failure this feature cannot\n50\t * absorb. The answer path's guards fail the OTHER way (toward refusing) and\n51\t * deliberately do not consult curation at all: a question captured before its\n52\t * thread was snoozed is still answerable.\n53\t */\n54\t\n55\timport * as fs from \"node:fs/promises\";\n56\timport * as os from \"node:os\";\n57\timport * as path from \"node:path\";\n58\timport Database from \"better-sqlite3\";\n59\timport { MULTI_REPO_ANCHORS_DIR } from \"../runtime/git/multi-repo\";\n60\timport { NON_GIT_BRANCH } from \"../runtime/git/non-git\";\n61\timport { agentKindFromAgentId } from \"./agent-kind\";\n62\timport type { AttemptLedger } from \"./attempt-ledger\";\n63\timport {\n64\t\tBRIDGE_CAPABILITIES,\n65\t\tBRIDGE_PROTOCOL_RANGE,"}]},"uuid":"10aff96d-6b88-4ab3-b57b-4a47068b8a26","timestamp":"2026-08-10T22:35:24.111Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\read-api.ts","content":"/**\n * (COMPANION-BRIDGE) — read endpoints: hello, tree, transcript, question,\n * heartbeat (§6.2, §7.2, §7.3, §7.4, §7.7).\n *\n * Reads mutate nothing and are therefore safe to retry. Note the naming\n * inversion this module has to live with: in CODE a *project* is the repo row in\n * the sidebar and a *workspace* is a branch/worktree; the user says these the\n * other way round. The protocol uses the CODE names and the client presents the\n * user's labels.\n *\n * Transcript text is sent VERBATIM. The bridge does not scrub secrets — a\n * partial scrub would be a false assurance. The confidentiality control is the\n * sealed envelope, not filtering.\n *\n * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n * WHAT THIS MODULE REFUSES TO INVENT\n * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n *  - There is no `green` / \"ready for review\" status and there never will be.\n *    The review axis lives in renderer storage the bridge cannot reach.\n *    `needs_input` (red), `working` (yellow) and `idle` (neutral) are the whole\n *    vocabulary; a fourth state synthesised from coarse data would be a lie.\n *  - No status decay ON A LIVE TERMINAL. A binding whose last event was `Start`\n *    three days ago is reported as `working`, because that is what the host\n *    actually recorded. Inventing a timeout would manufacture a state\n *    transition that never happened. (`TerminalAgentStore.clearWorkspaceStatuses`\n *    is the existing escape hatch for a wedged agent, and it runs on the host\n *    side.) This says NOTHING about a terminal that no longer exists — see\n *    `(BRIDGE-LIVENESS)` below, which is not decay but existence.\n *  - No guessed transcript when the agent session is unknown: the read fails\n *    loud rather than serving somebody else's conversation.\n *\n * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n * WHAT THIS MODULE FILTERS, AND IN WHICH DIRECTION IT FAILS\n * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n * Two filters stand between `host.db` and the phone, and they are independent:\n *\n *  - `(BRIDGE-SIDEBAR-FILTER)` — CURATION. The user's sidebar, projected into\n *    `host.db` by `(SIDEBAR-MIRROR)`: soft-deleted, completed, archived,\n *    snoozed and hidden threads are off the desktop's default sidebar and are\n *    therefore off the phone, and a repo the user removed from their sidebar\n *    takes its threads with it.\n *  - `(BRIDGE-LIVENESS)` — EXISTENCE. `status = 'active'` is not liveness; the\n *    daemon's own listing is. 403 rows on this machine matched the old\n *    predicate, 8 of them frozen on `PermissionRequest` and badging the phone\n *    with permanently-blocked agents that had not existed for weeks.\n *\n * BOTH FAIL TOWARD SHOWING. Uncertainty — an unfilled mirror, a workspace with\n * no mirrored row, an unreachable daemon, a stale snapshot — always renders the\n * row. Hiding a real blocked agent is the only failure this feature cannot\n * absorb. The answer path's guards fail the OTHER way (toward refusing) and\n * deliberately do not consult curation at all: a question captured before its\n * thread was snoozed is still answerable.\n */\n\nimport * as fs from \"node:fs/promises\";\nimport * as os from \"node:os\";\nimport * as path from \"node:path\";\nimport Database from \"better-sqlite3\";\nimport { MULTI_REPO_ANCHORS_DIR } from \"../runtime/git/multi-repo\";\nimport { NON_GIT_BRANCH } from \"../runtime/git/non-git\";\nimport { agentKindFromAgentId } from \"./agent-kind\";\nimport type { AttemptLedger } from \"./attempt-ledger\";\nimport {\n\tBRIDGE_CAPABILITIES,\n\tBRIDGE_PROTOCOL_RANGE,","numLines":65,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1417}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"62cc7a5f-d5a4-4414-aa79-b33b27b1e67a","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.226","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
