{"parentUuid":"0612b103-fa42-48ba-9f81-03901ed54fc8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0a8de032-5fd3-4106-bcf4-797ed6a2efc2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n\n   The user requires a “whole UX or fail loud” companion-answer contract:\n\n   - Any pending captured Claude question with a real terminal target must be answerable from a paired phone or watch.\n   - It must work when:\n     - the renderer is unavailable\n     - the display is off\n     - Windows is locked or at the login screen\n     - the transcript is unreadable, missing, rotated, or temporarily locked\n     - capability/session negotiation is missing or expired\n     - normal sidebar curation hides the thread\n     - mutable agent binding, permission-axis, AskUser marker, screen, or read-side liveness disagree\n   - No refusal or answer downgrade may depend on:\n     - transcript state/readability\n     - terminal screen/render state\n     - renderer availability\n     - Windows lock/login/display state\n     - mutable agent binding\n     - permission-axis state\n     - AskUser marker state\n     - read-side liveness\n     - negotiated companion answer capability/session state\n     - biometric/client claims\n     - post-write screen/transcript confirmation\n   - PTY outcomes must be honest:\n     - An acknowledged write is counted only after daemon-side `pty.write` is acknowledged.\n     - `confirmed` is returned only after all required acknowledged writes succeed and the durable ledger outcome is written and read back.\n     - If bytes may have landed but acknowledgment or durability is uncertain, return `unconfirmed` and retain the duplicate fence.\n     - Only a failure proving no bytes were written may be presented as zero-write/retryable.\n   - Pending questions must remain discoverable through `/v1/tree`, `/v1/question`, and heartbeat counts even if capability negotiation or sidebar curation would hide the thread.\n   - Positive transcript settlement after a desk answer must remain.\n   - Protocol 0 remains strictly read-only/no-write.\n\n   Boundaries that must remain:\n\n   - pairing and authenticated device identity\n   - Cloudflare Access validation\n   - sealed AES-GCM request/response transport\n   - nonce replay protection\n   - API schemas and semantic answer-shape validation\n   - exact current question ID/fingerprint check at the last synchronous point before writing\n   - answer-wide lease\n   - per-terminal lock\n   - durable request claim/idempotency/fencing\n   - actual daemon/PTTY failures\n   - honest zero-write and partial/unknown-write outcomes\n   - positive transcript settlement after desk answers\n   - protocol-0 no-write invariant\n\n   Operational requirements:\n\n   - Work directly on `main`.\n   - Never force-push.\n   - Merge remote differences without losing functionality.\n   - Ship only through the full GitHub Windows ARM64 build/release workflow.\n   - Never hot-patch the installed application.\n   - Do not install until the user explicitly authorizes installation at that exact time, because installation closes Superset and this session.\n   - Run `/simplify` fully before committing/pushing/reporting completion.\n   - Run `/code-review low` for every committed change batch.\n   - Use `tmp/` for scratch files.\n   - No UX answer barrier may be introduced without the user’s explicit approval.\n   - Security constraint preserved verbatim:\n     - “Never log free-text bodies, keys, tokens, or transcript content.”\n   - Never touch production database unless explicitly asked and confirmed.\n\n   Most recent explicit request:\n\n   - The user invoked `/simplify`.\n   - Its exact required workflow is:\n     - Phase 0 gather the diff.\n     - Phase 1 run four independent agents in parallel for reuse, simplification, efficiency, and altitude.\n     - Phase 2 deduplicate findings and directly apply all valid cleanups, skipping only findings that change intended behavior, require work well outside the diff, or are false positives.\n   - All four Phase 1 agents completed; Phase 2 is partially applied but not complete or validated.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n\n   - Windows ARM64 Superset fork:\n     - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64`\n   - Android/Wear companion:\n     - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion`\n   - Bun/Turbo TypeScript monorepo\n   - Host-service companion bridge\n   - Cloudflare Tunnel and Access JWT validation\n   - Per-device pairing and authenticated identity\n   - HKDF-derived directional keys\n   - AES-256-GCM sealed envelopes\n   - Method/path/protocol/status/nonce AAD binding\n   - Durable nonce replay protection\n   - Semantic answer intents instead of arbitrary terminal bytes\n   - Claude picker byte encoding\n   - Per-terminal locks\n   - Answer-wide leases\n   - Durable SQLite request claims and duplicate fencing\n   - PTY daemon protocol negotiation\n   - Protocol v3 correlated `input` / `input-ok` acknowledgments\n   - Protocol v2 detached-daemon compatibility\n   - Complete-sequence legacy fallback for v2\n   - `not_written` versus `unknown` transport outcomes\n   - Detached PTY daemon adoption after host-service restart\n   - Positive-only transcript reconciliation\n   - Cache-first transcript stat identity\n   - Sidebar curation escape for pending questions\n   - Heartbeat/tree parity\n   - Bun tests, scoped Biome, TypeScript diagnostics, REFERR-GATE\n   - Full GitHub Windows ARM64 packaging and release\n\n   Proven Claude picker contract for `claude-code@2.1.226`:\n\n   - Single-select: proven digit/review submission behavior.\n   - Free text in N>1 prompts: supported.\n   - Multi-select inside N>1 prompts: toggle digits followed by right-arrow.\n   - Multi-select free text: refused because live CLI runs committed the wrong option.\n   - Empty multi-select: refused because the CLI silently omits the question.\n   - No `\\r` may land inside a multi-select question except the proven final review-screen submission.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   A. Central answer path\n\n   - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer.ts`\n\n   Shipped in commit `ec83cf8e4`:\n\n   - The production answer path no longer invokes transcript/screen/session/binding/permission/marker guards.\n   - It:\n     1. durably claims the request\n     2. validates current pending question and fingerprint\n     3. semantically encodes the answer\n     4. prepares/adopts the PTY session outside the answer lease and lock\n     5. acquires the answer lease\n     6. acquires the terminal lock\n     7. rechecks exact current question/fingerprint\n     8. injects the sequence\n     9. records and reads back the durable result\n   - Exact current recheck occurs immediately before injection:\n     ```ts\n     requireCurrentPendingAnswerQuestion(deps, request);\n     return injectSequence(deps, {\n       question,\n       host,\n       keystrokes,\n       leaseId: lease.leaseId,\n       acknowledgedInputSupported:\n         prepared.acknowledgedInputSupported,\n       writer,\n     });\n     ```\n   - Durable outcome helper writes and reads back:\n     ```ts\n     async function recordOutcome(\n       deps: AnswerDeps,\n       record: AnswerAttemptRecord,\n     ): Promise<boolean> {\n       try {\n         if (record.status === \"in_flight\") return true;\n         deps.ledger.recordOutcome({\n           requestId: record.requestId,\n           status: record.status,\n           resolvedAtMs: record.resolvedAtMs,\n           failureCode: record.failureCode,\n           guardsPassed: record.guardsPassed,\n           leaseId: record.leaseId,\n         });\n         const durable = deps.ledger.get(record.requestId);\n         if (durable?.status !== record.status) {\n           throw new Error(\n             `ledger outcome verification read ${durable?.status ?? \"missing\"}, expected ${record.status}`,\n           );\n         }\n         return true;\n       } catch (error) {\n         deps.log({\n           event: \"companion.answer.attempt_persist_failed\",\n           requestId: record.requestId,\n           questionId: record.questionId,\n           status: record.status,\n           error: error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error),\n         });\n         return false;\n       }\n     }\n     ```\n   - Audit failure is non-vetoing:\n     ```ts\n     async function appendAnswerAudit(\n       deps: AnswerDeps,\n       entry: AuditEntry,\n     ): Promise<void> {\n       try {\n         await deps.audit.append(entry);\n       } catch (error) {\n         deps.log({\n           event: \"companion.answer.audit_persist_failed\",\n           requestId: entry.requestId,\n           questionId: entry.questionId,\n           terminalId: entry.terminalId,\n           outcome: entry.outcome,\n           error: error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error),\n         });\n       }\n     }\n     ```\n   - Injection result distinguishes definite zero-write from ambiguous outcomes:\n     ```ts\n     type InjectionResult =\n       | { kind: \"confirmed\" }\n       | {\n           kind: \"unconfirmed\";\n           reason: string;\n           abortedAt: number;\n           written: number;\n           writeOutcome: AcknowledgedInputFailureKind;\n         };\n     ```\n   - Only `written === 0 && writeOutcome === \"not_written\"` gets a retryable 503.\n   - `unknown`, including an ambiguous first write, marks the question stale, returns durable `unconfirmed`, and preserves the duplicate fence.\n   - Preparation/adoption now occurs before lease/lock:\n     ```ts\n     const writer = rawWriterFor(deps);\n     const prepared = await writer.prepare({\n       terminalId: host.hostTerminalId,\n       workspaceId: host.hostWorkspaceId,\n     });\n     ```\n   - Preparation failures are logged without sensitive bodies and become definite zero-write/retryable failures.\n\n   Latest uncommitted `/simplify` edits:\n\n   - Replaced the safety-critical boolean parameter:\n     ```ts\n     requirePendingAnswerQuestion(deps, request, true);\n     ```\n     with a named wrapper:\n     ```ts\n     function requireCurrentPendingAnswerQuestion(\n       deps: AnswerDeps,\n       request: Pick<AnswerRequest, \"questionId\" | \"fingerprint\">,\n     ): PendingQuestion\n     ```\n   - Imported and reused:\n     ```ts\n     import type { AcknowledgedInputFailureKind } from \"../terminal/DaemonClient\";\n     ```\n   - Began simplifying `injectSequence` from duplicate v2/v3 branches into one frame loop:\n     ```ts\n     const frames = acknowledgedInputSupported\n       ? keystrokes.map((keystroke, index) => ({\n           data: keystroke.data,\n           acknowledgedKeystrokes: 1,\n           abortAt: index,\n         }))\n       : keystrokes.length === 0\n         ? []\n         : [{\n             data: keystrokes.map((keystroke) => keystroke.data).join(\"\"),\n             acknowledgedKeystrokes: keystrokes.length,\n             abortAt: keystrokes.length,\n           }];\n     ```\n   - Both v3 per-keystroke frames and the one-frame v2 sequence now share the same deadline, lease extension, write, error log, and abort loop.\n   - The duplicate legacy branch and dead `written = keystrokes.length` assignment were removed.\n   - This uncommitted rewrite has not yet been formatted or tested.\n\n   Important dead-code cleanup under consideration:\n\n   - `/simplify` found the historical guard evaluator is now fully dead in production:\n     - `GUARD_CLASSES`\n     - `ABSTAINING_GUARDS`\n     - `LOAD_BEARING_GUARDS`\n     - `GUARD_EVALUATION_ORDER`\n     - `assertGuardClassification`\n     - `evaluateGuards`\n     - `mergeAttemptEvidence`\n     - screen guard verification tree\n     - guard-specific adapters\n   - The file header already states:\n     ```ts\n     Legacy guard-analysis helpers remain temporarily for historical tests.\n     They have no production caller...\n     ```\n   - Removal had not yet been performed when compaction was requested.\n   - `/v1/message` still needs screen/composer helpers such as `safeSnapshot` and `screenShowsPickerChrome`; those must not be deleted with the dead answer guards.\n\n   B. Raw writer contract\n\n   - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\keystrokes.ts`\n\n   Shipped contract:\n\n   ```ts\n   export interface RawWriteTarget {\n     terminalId: string;\n     workspaceId: string;\n   }\n\n   export interface RawWriteInput extends RawWriteTarget {\n     data: string;\n   }\n\n   export type RawPrepareResult =\n     | { success: true; acknowledgedInputSupported: boolean }\n     | { error: string };\n\n   export type RawWriteResult =\n     | { success: true }\n     | {\n         error: string;\n         writeOutcome: \"not_written\" | \"unknown\";\n       };\n   ```\n\n   - The writer is branded so paste framing or unvalidated fire-and-forget cannot be wired accidentally.\n   - `prepare` performs detached-session adoption before the final current-question check.\n\n   Latest uncommitted `/simplify` edit:\n\n   ```ts\n   import type { AcknowledgedInputFailureKind } from \"../terminal/DaemonClient\";\n   ```\n\n   and:\n\n   ```ts\n   writeOutcome: AcknowledgedInputFailureKind;\n   ```\n\n   This deduplicates the outcome union.\n\n   C. Daemon client\n\n   - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\terminal\\DaemonClient\\DaemonClient.ts`\n\n   - Defines:\n     ```ts\n     export type AcknowledgedInputFailureKind = \"not_written\" | \"unknown\";\n\n     export class AcknowledgedInputError extends Error {\n       readonly writeOutcome: AcknowledgedInputFailureKind;\n\n       constructor(\n         message: string,\n         writeOutcome: AcknowledgedInputFailureKind,\n       ) {\n         super(message);\n         this.name = \"AcknowledgedInputError\";\n         this.writeOutcome = writeOutcome;\n       }\n     }\n     ```\n   - Explicit class field was required because Node `--experimental-strip-types` cannot parse TypeScript parameter properties.\n   - Handshake offers all supported protocols:\n     ```ts\n     this.send({\n       type: \"hello\",\n       protocols: [...SUPPORTED_PROTOCOL_VERSIONS],\n     });\n     ```\n   - v3:\n     - sends correlated `requestId`\n     - waits for `input-ok`\n     - correlated daemon error is `not_written`\n     - timeout/disconnect after queue is `unknown`\n   - v2:\n     - queues the supplied legacy input frame\n     - returns/throws `unknown`\n     - `injectSequence` passes the entire encoded sequence in one frame, so a free-text or multi-select answer is not truncated after the first keystroke\n   - `AcknowledgedInputError` strip-types parsing was independently rechecked.\n\n   `/simplify` finding not yet applied:\n\n   - `requestInput`, `requestSession`, and `requestNonSession` duplicate request/reply listener/timer cleanup scaffolding.\n   - Refactoring them into a generic `awaitReply` was considered risky because the code is timing-sensitive and owns `not_written` versus `unknown` semantics.\n   - Likely skip unless implemented with careful tests.\n\n   D. Terminal session preparation and write\n\n   - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\terminal\\terminal.ts`\n\n   Shipped preparation:\n\n   ```ts\n   export async function prepareAcknowledgedInputSession({\n     terminalId,\n     workspaceId,\n     db,\n   }): Promise<\n     | { success: true; acknowledgedInputSupported: boolean }\n     | { error: string }\n   >\n   ```\n\n   - Calls `getOrAdoptSession`.\n   - Catches adoption/setup exceptions before any input frame.\n   - Returns definite zero-write failures.\n   - Exposes whether the negotiated daemon can acknowledge input.\n\n   Shipped write:\n\n   ```ts\n   export async function writeAcknowledgedInputToSession({\n     terminalId,\n     workspaceId,\n     data,\n   }): Promise<\n     | { success: true }\n     | { error: string; writeOutcome: AcknowledgedInputFailureKind }\n   >\n   ```\n\n   - Uses only the already-prepared process-local session.\n   - No host.db/daemon listing/replay I/O occurs after the final identity check.\n   - Actual daemon write errors preserve `not_written` versus `unknown`.\n\n   Latest uncommitted `/simplify` edits:\n\n   - Imported:\n     ```ts\n     type AcknowledgedInputFailureKind\n     ```\n   - Added shared:\n     ```ts\n     function writableSession(\n       terminalId: string,\n       workspaceId: string,\n     ): TerminalSession | { error: string }\n     ```\n   - Both ordinary and acknowledged writers now reuse that precondition helper.\n   - `prepareAcknowledgedInputSession` also reuses the helper after adoption.\n   - Removed the unused `eventBus` argument from preparation because the only caller never supplied it.\n   - These edits have not yet been formatted/tested.\n\n   E. Composition root\n\n   - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\index.ts`\n\n   Shipped wiring:\n\n   ```ts\n   const writeInput = Object.assign(\n     (input: RawWriteInput) => writeAcknowledgedInputToSession(input),\n     {\n       writerKind: RAW_PTY_WRITER_KIND,\n       prepare: (input: RawWriteTarget) =>\n         prepareAcknowledgedInputSession({ ...input, db: deps.db }),\n     },\n   );\n   ```\n\n   - Binds prepare/adoption to host.db.\n   - Prevents adoption from occurring inside the final critical write window.\n   - Historical transcript and marker guard adapters are still present despite no production answer caller.\n   - `/simplify` found those dead adapters should be removed if the dead guard subsystem is deleted.\n\n   F. PTY protocol and daemon\n\n   - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\pty-daemon\\src\\protocol\\version.ts`\n\n   ```ts\n   export const CURRENT_PROTOCOL_VERSION = 3 as const;\n   export const SUPPORTED_PROTOCOL_VERSIONS: readonly number[] = [3, 2];\n   ```\n\n   - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\pty-daemon\\package.json`\n     - bumped from `0.3.0` to `0.4.0`\n   - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\bun.lock`\n     - updated workspace version\n   - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\pty-daemon\\src\\Server\\Server.ts`\n     - rejects request-ID acknowledged input on negotiated v2 with `EPROTO`\n   - v2 remains available for ordinary terminal operations and the controlled complete-sequence legacy fallback.\n   - v3 gives true daemon-side acknowledgment.\n\n   G. Daemon supervisor and tests\n\n   - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\daemon\\DaemonSupervisor.ts`\n     - probes with `[3, 2]`\n     - can identify a v2 daemon’s package version\n     - marks old daemon `updatePending`\n   - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\daemon\\DaemonSupervisor.test.ts`\n     - proves v2 is probeable/adoptable\n     - proves v2 companion input is queued and returns `unknown`\n     - proves stale daemon gets update-pending status\n\n   H. Transcript reconciliation\n\n   - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\question-store.ts`\n\n   Shipped behavior:\n\n   - Positive transcript `tool_result` settles a desk answer.\n   - `unreadable` is never cached as a terminal verdict.\n   - Reconciliation arbitrates after async reads using:\n     ```ts\n     store.resolve(\n       question.questionId,\n       { deviceLabel: null, surface: \"desktop\" },\n       nowMs,\n     )\n     ```\n   - This prevents a delayed transcript scan from:\n     - overwriting phone provenance\n     - resurrecting a stale question\n     - firing settlement twice\n\n   Latest uncommitted `/simplify` edit:\n\n   - Reworded stale guard-era comment:\n     ```ts\n     SUBAGENT id when a subagent asked; `null` on the main loop. Retained for\n     internal ownership diagnostics and never sent to a client.\n     ```\n\n   `/simplify` efficiency findings not yet applied:\n\n   - The reconcile stat cache keys on size/mtime, so active transcripts can miss every heartbeat and reread/reparse up to 8 MiB.\n   - Per-question transcript reads are serial.\n   - Proposed incremental growth-aware scanning is risky because partial JSONL lines, rotation, shrink, and tail-window semantics must remain exact.\n   - Parallel scans could multiply concurrent 8 MiB allocations.\n   - Likely skip in this cleanup because those changes alter behavior/performance architecture beyond safe simplification.\n\n   I. Discovery and curation\n\n   - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\read-api.ts`\n\n   Shipped behavior:\n\n   - Pending-question terminals pierce workspace/project curation.\n   - Pending refs appear even without `tree.read`.\n   - `/v1/question` no longer needs `question.read`.\n   - Heartbeat applies the same curation exception as tree.\n\n   Latest uncommitted `/simplify` edits:\n\n   ```ts\n   function terminalPiercesCuration(\n     visibleWorkspaces: ReadonlySet<string>,\n     workspaceId: string,\n     pending: PendingQuestion | null,\n   ): boolean {\n     return visibleWorkspaces.has(workspaceId) || pending !== null;\n   }\n   ```\n\n   - Both tree and heartbeat count loops now call this shared predicate.\n   - Deleted redundant:\n     ```ts\n     if (!visible.has(row.id) && all.length === 0) continue;\n     ```\n     because the later `shown.length === 0` check already drops the same workspace.\n   - Larger altitude proposal to fold pending admission into `visibleWorkspaces` was not applied because it would change curation provenance and hidden-count semantics.\n\n   J. HTTP/protocol boundary\n\n   - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\http.ts`\n\n   - `/v1/answer`, `/v1/answer/status`, `/v1/question`, `/v1/tree`, heartbeat, hello, and panic are capability-null at route policy.\n   - Path validation uses the opened request protocol version:\n     ```ts\n     requireProtocolPath(path, opened.protocolVersion);\n     ```\n   - Protocol 0 permits only hello/tree/heartbeat.\n   - `/v1/answer` and `/v1/panic` remain blocked under protocol 0.\n   - `confirmedBiometric` is optional and ignored, but malformed supplied values remain schema-invalid.\n\n   K. Feature manifest\n\n   - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\FEATURES.md`\n\n   `(ANSWER-GUARDLESS)` documents:\n\n   - pending question discovery without session/capability\n   - curation escape\n   - no transcript/screen/renderer/login/session/binding/permission/marker/liveness/capability veto\n   - display-off/locked-screen behavior\n   - daemon acknowledgment and durable outcome behavior\n   - detached v2 behavior:\n     - entire encoded sequence in one ordered legacy frame\n     - zero acknowledged writes counted\n     - durable `unconfirmed`\n     - stale question\n     - duplicate fence\n     - never false `confirmed`\n     - never truncates after the first keystroke\n\n   L. Tests and scratch probe\n\n   - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer-guardless.test.ts`\n     - guardless direct injection\n     - no biometric gate\n     - true zero-write\n     - ambiguous first-write\n     - partial write\n     - full v2 sequence in one frame\n   - Latest uncommitted `/simplify` edit:\n     - callback uses `RawWriteResult` rather than retyping the union.\n   - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\answer-guardless-probe.test.ts`\n     - scratch-only, not committed\n     - end-to-end fake-ledger probes:\n       - confirmed path\n       - replay fencing\n       - zero-write retry\n       - ambiguous first write\n       - partial write\n       - supersede under lock\n       - confirmed ledger failure\n       - both outcome writes failing\n       - audit failure\n       - preparation failure and fresh retry\n       - supersede during preparation\n   - Last run:\n     - 11 pass, 0 fail\n\n   M. Dead historical guard test\n\n   - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\guard-abstain.test.ts`\n   - Read in full during current `/simplify`.\n   - Contains historical tests for:\n     - `GUARD_CLASSES`\n     - `ABSTAINING_GUARDS`\n     - `LOAD_BEARING_GUARDS`\n     - `GUARD_EVALUATION_ORDER`\n     - `evaluateGuards`\n     - `mergeAttemptEvidence`\n     - legacy replay guard evidence\n   - No production answer code uses those evaluators now.\n   - File had not yet been deleted or rewritten when compaction was requested.\n\n4. Errors and Fixes:\n\n   - Original phone refusal:\n     - “Failed — The desktop refused: the question wasn’t safely on screen”\n     - `guard transcript failed`\n     - Fixed by removing production answer guard evaluation.\n\n   - Fire-and-forget daemon enqueue was treated as success:\n     - Fixed with protocol-v3 correlated `input-ok` after daemon-side `pty.write`.\n\n   - Confirmed outcome could be returned before durable outcome verification:\n     - Fixed with ledger readback and downgrade to durable/fenced `unconfirmed`.\n\n   - Audit sink failure could block input or replace partial-write outcome:\n     - Fixed with non-vetoing `appendAnswerAudit`.\n\n   - Transient transcript unreadability was cached:\n     - Fixed by never caching/reusing `unreadable`.\n\n   - `/v1/question` was capability/session gated:\n     - Fixed