v1/message` screen helpers and legacy ledger schema.\n   - Decide whether to centralize repeated attempt-record/audit settlement blocks.\n   - Likely skip generic DaemonClient request scaffolding refactor due timing/transport risk.\n   - Likely skip transcript incremental/parallel scan changes due behavioral and memory risk.\n   - Likely keep two-stage writer branding because it validates a critical API boundary, unless replaced by a safer single factory.\n   - Likely skip moving curation admission into `visibleWorkspaces` because it changes provenance/hidden-count behavior.\n\n6. All User Messages:\n\n   Genuine earlier user messages preserved from prior context:\n\n   - `/compact`\n   - “This desktop is too old to answer this kind of question from here. i didn't answer the existing adams email thread still open for an hour and it gave me this. I didn't approve this barrier. remove all barriers, if I can answer in the terminal I want the phone to be able to handle it. end of story, stop building stupid safety mechanisms for this 1 person app”\n   - “i typed in an askuser and gpt yhis Unconfirmed - the desktop accepted the write but did not confirm the outcome”\n   - “This may or may not have gone through. Nothing will be sent again - checking reads the outcome from the desktop... this is bullshit how far can it be to type in a box... why are we getting these errors.. the question remained unanswered still I'm gonna do it on desktop now... make sure everything has heavy logging so you can tackle everything 1st shot”\n   - Empty multi-select choice: “Refuse w/ message (Recommended)”\n   - “I couldn't even respond on my watch it said desktop bridge wouldn't allow - wtf is this man... I need to kill all barriers to my perfect ux - follow simple rule if there is a question in terminal I need to be able to answer phone or watch - no blockers without my explciti approval per blocker (currently I want none and we add over time)”\n   - Desktop install choice: “Later”\n   - Biometric choice: “Drop biometric gate (Recommended)”\n   - ADB endpoints: “phone 56:40921    watch 67:39025”\n   - Updated phone port: “56:46199”\n   - Earlier installer authorization: “Install now (Recommended)”\n   - “all installed now - do you need to do e2e testing on your emulated versions etc?”\n   - `/compact` followed by “Continue from where you left off.”\n   - Screenshot complaint:\n     - “dude what is this? I thought you I told you to get rid of all the guards. it's killing the ux. I need to be able to respond. In every scenario no matter what. that chat is still open so you can emulate right now. I wanted to choose option one if you need to test.”\n   - “it needs to work even if the screen is off and I need to enter my password to open it again”\n   - “get sol and fable to thoroughly review the approach - use emulators to test where possible”\n   - “please confirm that this issue will be resolved as well. by this, you better make sure from logs that you're really tackling the root cause ux comes first. these guards need to be killed off... generally make sweeping changes to kill the odds of my messages not being able to get through”\n   - “if you need to test that question is still open, I'd like to choose the option that gives us a one-off script in the CWD”\n\n   Security/operational constraints from the user:\n\n   - “Never log free-text bodies, keys, tokens, or transcript content.”\n   - Never touch production database unless explicitly asked and confirmed.\n   - Ship through the full GitHub Windows ARM64 build/release path; never hot-patch.\n   - Install only after explicit user authorization at the exact time because installation closes Superset and the session.\n   - No UX answer barrier may be added without explicit user approval.\n\n   User messages in the current continuation:\n\n   - A continuation message containing the prior compaction summary and:\n     - “Continue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any furthe