{"parentUuid":"34db1087-00f7-4834-a194-e14a86bc41f5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"bde165d4-0a57-45fb-836f-f4a982318cf7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_lykdcHzZfT45zAEP79o1VqQR","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Memory Index\n2\t\n3\t- [GUARD5 answer-path fix: phone answers were ALL refused](project_companion_guard5_answer_path_fix.md) — 2026-08-08/09, THREE batches on pty-proven 2.1.226 contracts; 08-09 (builds 31330145092): MSEL-N2-PROVEN (multiSelect in N>1 = toggle digits then \\x1b[C any position, NEVER \\r inside a multi group; old refutation was only the N=1 tail pair), guard-4 permission_axis fully abstains (vetoed 2/2 free-text answers mid-write on weak same_prompt keystrokes), mergeAttemptEvidence (abstains union across keystrokes), empty multiSelect refused w/ message (CLI silently drops the question — user-chosen), guard-5 clip check armed for multi via detection-only \"[ ] Type something\" needle; earlier: free-text all shapes, SESSION-REHELLO phone fix, phone-protocol EMULATOR tmp/phone-emu/ (closed-loop E2E); multiSelect free-text stays refused (CLI commits wrong option); ~45 findings, every review round found something real\n4\t\n5\t- [WATCHER-BLUE-STOMP: blue dot lost after /compact](project_watcher_blue_stomp.md) — SHIPPED 2026-08-06 (6 commits bbcda086f..0f0537066, 6 Opus+Sol review rounds, build 31127061903): replay gate (uuid+age) + exact interrupt sentinel (phrase-grep matched QUOTES → false mid-turn Stops); watcher owns ONLY interrupts, hook's StopFailure owns terminal api-errors; blobs are pure LF (autocrlf warning ≠ CRLF blobs); on green → download installer + detached self-install (explicit go given)\n6\t\n7\t- [superset-companion planning](project_superset_companion_planning.md) — Android/Wear app answering blocked agents from the wrist; OVERHAUL SHIPPED 2026-08-06 (presence-gated push, sidebar mirror, bridge filters/liveness, restart-safe fences, registration+watchdog hardening, curated phone UI; fork ddc96e1aa / phone cfaf456, both APKs sideloaded) — next session runs the POST-INSTALL VERIFICATION LIST in this file; proven picker byte contract, ACP rejected\n8\t- [Companion durability moved to host.db](project_companion_durability_hostdb.md) — attempt ledger + replay cache + device index are rows now (NTFS rename is not crash-atomic on win32); answer_attempts is NEVER pruned because every row is a fence; the 3x \"legacy state read conditionally, deleted unconditionally\" bug class; shipped desktop-v1.18.1\n9\t- [Companion verification recipes + traps](reference_companion_verification_recipes.md) — quoted heredocs EAT backslash escapes here (use Write + python file); bun:sqlite shim EBUSY is expected; FileShare.None is the only real Windows handle detector; differential vectors need run-differential.ps1\n10\t- [Android/JDK toolchain (portable, ARM64)](reference_android_toolchain_portable_arm64.md) — ~/dev-tools holds native aarch64 JDK 21 + Android SDK 36; winget exit 1602 = silent UAC, use portable zips; Git Bash lies about arch (says AMD64 on an ARM64 box); already-running processes never see newly-persisted User env vars\n11\t\n12\t- [Opus + Sol + Fable subagents for all work/reviews](feedback_opus_sol_subagents_all_work.md) — 2026-08-06: Opus subagents default executor for EVERYTHING; code reviews = Opus + Sol ONLY, save Fable usage wherever possible; kill finished agents\n13\t\n14\t- [DEAD-BUS: AskUser red lost + facepile chip removal](project_askuser_red_lost_monitor_stomp.md) — yellow-not-red ROOT-CAUSED: renderer WS event bus dead 7h43m after host-service restart (fire-and-forget broadcast + reconnect replays only fs:watch + suspected stale-PSK 5-min retry loop); MONITOR-STOMP disproved; fix = reconnect state-snapshot reconcile + PSK refresh + disconnected indicator; also full silent-drop-point map of the PermissionRequest path; red-\"2\" = upstream agents facepile chip (unfixed pre-CHIP-DOT-UNIFY status copy), user chose remove outright → (AGENTS-CHIP-REMOVED)\n15\t- [Prove unknowns before building](feedback_planning_prove_before_building.md) — planning is its own phase: PROOF agents run real commands, VIEWPOINT agents (different models) attack the design, no code until told\n16\t\n17\t- [Electric v2Workspaces dead for new rows](project_electric_v2workspaces_dead_for_new_rows.md) — upstream v1.16 offline-first: new workspaces exist only in host.db (cloud_synced_at null, no reconciler shipped); anything reading collections.v2Workspaces misses them → Kanban blind to post-upgrade threads; use useHostWorkspaces()\n18\t\n19\t- [TAB-CHIPS + crash hunt](project_tab_chips_and_crash_hunt.md) — sidebar per-tab chips + FORK-LEDGER/BG-STALE-BLUE dot fixes shipped desktop-v1.16.1; host-service 0xC0000409 crashloop OPEN (onnxruntime suspect, WER dumps armed, dump-first-then-fix)\n20\t"}]},"uuid":"551ef119-e53d-4154-a13f-55f718dbca94","timestamp":"2026-08-11T00:09:05.956Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\khair\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\memory\\MEMORY.md","content":"# Memory Index\n\n- [GUARD5 answer-path fix: phone answers were ALL refused](project_companion_guard5_answer_path_fix.md) — 2026-08-08/09, THREE batches on pty-proven 2.1.226 contracts; 08-09 (builds 31330145092): MSEL-N2-PROVEN (multiSelect in N>1 = toggle digits then \\x1b[C any position, NEVER \\r inside a multi group; old refutation was only the N=1 tail pair), guard-4 permission_axis fully abstains (vetoed 2/2 free-text answers mid-write on weak same_prompt keystrokes), mergeAttemptEvidence (abstains union across keystrokes), empty multiSelect refused w/ message (CLI silently drops the question — user-chosen), guard-5 clip check armed for multi via detection-only \"[ ] Type something\" needle; earlier: free-text all shapes, SESSION-REHELLO phone fix, phone-protocol EMULATOR tmp/phone-emu/ (closed-loop E2E); multiSelect free-text stays refused (CLI commits wrong option); ~45 findings, every review round found something real\n\n- [WATCHER-BLUE-STOMP: blue dot lost after /compact](project_watcher_blue_stomp.md) — SHIPPED 2026-08-06 (6 commits bbcda086f..0f0537066, 6 Opus+Sol review rounds, build 31127061903): replay gate (uuid+age) + exact interrupt sentinel (phrase-grep matched QUOTES → false mid-turn Stops); watcher owns ONLY interrupts, hook's StopFailure owns terminal api-errors; blobs are pure LF (autocrlf warning ≠ CRLF blobs); on green → download installer + detached self-install (explicit go given)\n\n- [superset-companion planning](project_superset_companion_planning.md) — Android/Wear app answering blocked agents from the wrist; OVERHAUL SHIPPED 2026-08-06 (presence-gated push, sidebar mirror, bridge filters/liveness, restart-safe fences, registration+watchdog hardening, curated phone UI; fork ddc96e1aa / phone cfaf456, both APKs sideloaded) — next session runs the POST-INSTALL VERIFICATION LIST in this file; proven picker byte contract, ACP rejected\n- [Companion durability moved to host.db](project_companion_durability_hostdb.md) — attempt ledger + replay cache + device index are rows now (NTFS rename is not crash-atomic on win32); answer_attempts is NEVER pruned because every row is a fence; the 3x \"legacy state read conditionally, deleted unconditionally\" bug class; shipped desktop-v1.18.1\n- [Companion verification recipes + traps](reference_companion_verification_recipes.md) — quoted heredocs EAT backslash escapes here (use Write + python file); bun:sqlite shim EBUSY is expected; FileShare.None is the only real Windows handle detector; differential vectors need run-differential.ps1\n- [Android/JDK toolchain (portable, ARM64)](reference_android_toolchain_portable_arm64.md) — ~/dev-tools holds native aarch64 JDK 21 + Android SDK 36; winget exit 1602 = silent UAC, use portable zips; Git Bash lies about arch (says AMD64 on an ARM64 box); already-running processes never see newly-persisted User env vars\n\n- [Opus + Sol + Fable subagents for all work/reviews](feedback_opus_sol_subagents_all_work.md) — 2026-08-06: Opus subagents default executor for EVERYTHING; code reviews = Opus + Sol ONLY, save Fable usage wherever possible; kill finished agents\n\n- [DEAD-BUS: AskUser red lost + facepile chip removal](project_askuser_red_lost_monitor_stomp.md) — yellow-not-red ROOT-CAUSED: renderer WS event bus dead 7h43m after host-service restart (fire-and-forget broadcast + reconnect replays only fs:watch + suspected stale-PSK 5-min retry loop); MONITOR-STOMP disproved; fix = reconnect state-snapshot reconcile + PSK refresh + disconnected indicator; also full silent-drop-point map of the PermissionRequest path; red-\"2\" = upstream agents facepile chip (unfixed pre-CHIP-DOT-UNIFY status copy), user chose remove outright → (AGENTS-CHIP-REMOVED)\n- [Prove unknowns before building](feedback_planning_prove_before_building.md) — planning is its own phase: PROOF agents run real commands, VIEWPOINT agents (different models) attack the design, no code until told\n\n- [Electric v2Workspaces dead for new rows](project_electric_v2workspaces_dead_for_new_rows.md) — upstream v1.16 offline-first: new workspaces exist only in host.db (cloud_synced_at null, no reconciler shipped); anything reading collections.v2Workspaces misses them → Kanban blind to post-upgrade threads; use useHostWorkspaces()\n\n- [TAB-CHIPS + crash hunt](project_tab_chips_and_crash_hunt.md) — sidebar per-tab chips + FORK-LEDGER/BG-STALE-BLUE dot fixes shipped desktop-v1.16.1; host-service 0xC0000409 crashloop OPEN (onnxruntime suspect, WER dumps armed, dump-first-then-fix)\n","numLines":20,"startLine":1,"totalLines":58}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"34db1087-00f7-4834-a194-e14a86bc41f5","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.226","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"d8b12f94-b446-40d3-bad7-27b8534947ad","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"bde165d4-0a57-45fb-836f-f4a982318cf7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_hVN8gqq3ckabiHfHEfQ8Cjh4","type":"tool_result","content":"Task #3: Verify and ship the guardless path\nStatus: in_progress\nDescription: Add/adjust tests for locked or off-screen desktop operation, run required scoped validation and reviews, commit directly to main, push, and start the full GitHub build for installation later."}]},"uuid":"79d07ef5-4932-4935-810b-5f2bb9be04a7","timestamp":"2026-08-11T00:09:06.184Z","toolUseResult":{"task":{"id":"3","subject":"Verify and ship the guardless path","description":"Add/adjust tests for locked or off-screen desktop operation, run required scoped validation and reviews, commit directly to main, push, and start the full GitHub build for installation later.","status":"in_progress","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d8b12f94-b446-40d3-bad7-27b8534947ad","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.226","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"53a9c876-b1d0-44c5-9c24-80e83af60f76","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"bde165d4-0a57-45fb-836f-f4a982318cf7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_j0MQmGdO1EYA4R14yWDNsXbo","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: companion-guard5-answer-path-fix\n3\tdescription: \"GUARD5 answer-path overhaul 2026-08-08: why every phone answer was refused, the 8-commit fix batch, the pty-proven 2.1.226 picker contract, and what is still refused by design\"\n4\tmetadata: \n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: project\n7\t  originSessionId: 41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91\n8\t  modified: 2026-08-10T14:53:30.750Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\t**Shipped 2026-08-08** (fork commits `10be67f65..d8eaa299a`, 8 commits pushed to main, build 31260063144 dispatched; rebuilds desktop-v1.19.0 in place). Root cause of \"The desktop refused: the question wasn't safely on screen\" on EVERY phone answer: guard 5's band check assumed option rows are adjacent lines, but real pickers render wrapped descriptions between rows (4 rows span 9-11 lines). Second barrier: 8-char label floor refused short labels (\"Skip\") upstream documents as the normal shape. Third: free-text row label drifted \"Other\"→\"Type something.\" (2.1.220→2.1.226). Lifetime answer_attempts before fix: 0 confirmed.\n12\t\n13\t**The fix shape (all in packages/host-service/src/companion/):** picker-block invariant — ascending line-anchored digit rows, each inter-row gap explained by the option-above's description ACTUALLY matched on screen (longest-matched-prefix budget, binary search over includes; never capture-claimed length), display-cell width vs screen-derived cols, memoised exhaustive placement search (digits repeat across N-question blocks; greedy strands rows). Evidence tiers: pressed row strong (label floor OR own description strictly in its own region — next row's line excluded), others digit-consistent, ≥1 strong option row at the accepted placement (enforced ONLY in rowsFormPickerBlock's sawStrongRow — a from:0 pre-check degenerated under the region clamp into a partial-write hazard on multiSelect: toggles written, submit refused). Free-text row: exact raw-line end-bounded match (no squash/case-fold — impostor options \"TYPE SOMETHING.\" must refuse), two-candidates=refuse, bound into the accepted placement. `PICKER_CONTRACTS` versioned map owns bytes+copy per CLI build; producer AND validator share `provenFreeTextRowLabel()` (they diverged once → validateCapture rejected EVERY normal capture at ingestion — the label is used in the capture cross-check, so the sink and store must derive from one constant).\n14\t\n15\t**Pty-proven on claude-code@2.1.226** (11 live pickers, tool_result ground truth; harness tmp/refusal-2026-08-08/pty_canary_node.mjs — MUST run under node, node-pty dies under Bun ERR_SOCKET_CLOSED): single-select ONE bare digit selects+submits; free-text = [digit N+1, text, \\r] (digit opens inline editor — a \"focused-not-open\" scare was an under-determined screen read; typed tool_result is the only ground truth); multiSelect: digits/space toggle, ENTER TOGGLES-NOT-SUBMITS, \\x1b[C opens a review screen then \\r submits; multiSelect DOES render free-text row \"Type something\" (no period) + chat row (old !multiSelect folklore wrong); \"Chat about this\" at N+2 in all pickers, sentinel __chat__, digits 1..N unshifted; N-question numbering restarts per question. TUI emits ESC[nC instead of spaces — naive ANSI strip breaks needles; replay through @xterm/headless.\n16\t\n17\t**Still refused by design (not bugs):** free-text on N>1 prompts (59% of traffic — biggest open UX gap, needs driven editor proof), multiSelect free-text, option indices >9, clipped-viewport (picker taller than window → row_absent). Runtime drift detector (proven-version.ts) reports installed-CLI-vs-PROVEN_AGAINST on companion.gate — memoise ONLY successful reads (a cached null suppressed the warning forever). Open follow-ups: guard-4 permission_axis flaky latch, stale armed fence row Jg3tdkW8zw2lcMBkiKyyqw w/ missing transcript, be9a2256e's commit message falsely claims free-text contract known-wrong (retracted in 9a3ff0c13).\n18\t\n19\t**Process notes that paid:** live E2E before shipping — stage-1 dry-run harness (tmp/refusal-2026-08-08/e2e_answer_harness.ts) runs real matcher+encoder against the live viewport via terminal.snapshot/writeInput tRPC (manifest Bearer; response is superjson: result.data.json); it caught that the user's \"same chat\" was a DIFFERENT terminal (always resolve the pending tool_use, never trust a stale terminal id). Review cycle: 2 reviewers → fix → 2 fresh verifiers → fix → spot-check found NEW bugs every round incl. a BLOCKER introduced BY a fix; ~28 verified findings total. Answer path proven live twice (option A raw write; option B via full patched-guard harness).\n20\t\n21\t**SESSION-REHELLO (same day, after reinstall): the \"This desktop can't take that — answer at the desk\" error at question-OPEN is a DIFFERENT bug** — bridge sessions are in-memory; desktop restart wipes them; the phone cached its wireSession for the 1h TTL and never re-helloed (§6.3 was specced but unimplemented), so every gated route 501'd capability_unsupported for up to an hour after EVERY restart while ungated tree/heartbeat kept the app looking healthy. Fixed phone-side `9b9aae2`+`a6dcd98` (discard on restart-detect + on capability 501; sessions BOUND to bridge lifetime via first beat — only a session predating the observed lifetime is stale; identity-scoped compare-and-set invalidation under one lock so a delayed S0 error can't clear fresh S1) — both APKs sideloaded 2026-08-08 evening. Fork hardening `af4994acd` (pushed, ships next build): dead session now gets distinct sealed 409 session_expired instead of masquerading as 501. LIVE RESTART TEST STILL PENDING: next Superset restart → open phone app → answer a question (one retry allowed in the rare hello-vs-first-beat race).\n22\t\n23\t**COMPLETION BATCH (same day, evening — 6 more commits 2de601b67..9c42a38c2 pushed, build 31278552490):** (FREETEXT-N2-PROVEN) free-text ENABLED on N>1 all-single-select prompts — pty-proven per-question groups [digit N+1, text, \\r] which ADVANCE (free-text on last question = two consecutive \\r; final \\r on review screen submits); multiSelect free-text REFUTED not just unproven (terminal swallows the text and commits the caret row — proven wrong-answer), multiSelect-inside-N>1 REFUTED (\\x1b[C means \"Next\" there → selects a question never asked) — both stay refused forever unless upstream changes. (GUARD5-CLIPPED-VIEWPORT) prefix/suffix clips accepted when the clipped edge is affirmatively explained (endsWith-positional suffix match — `includes` was a proven forgery hole; clip needle floor = 12) and the pressed row is visible+strong. (GUARD4-ABSTAIN) permission_axis abstains ONLY on strong item_picker keystrokes when all load-bearing guards passed (weak same_prompt keystrokes keep refusal — matchPromptStillOnScreen matches a picker-GONE echo); abstain is a distinct outcome threaded through ledger/audit/wire; replay derives it (null = cannot say). (PUSH-ORPHAN-GONE/STALE-VERDICT) orphan fence verdict tri-state resolved|unresolved|gone (gone = projects root AND slug dir stat + transcript ENOENT → retire without buzz) with generation-checked async currency (adoption/deadline race was losing live notifications). ~40 verified review findings total across the day, every serious one executed not argued. Review cadence that worked: 2 reviewers → fix → 2 fresh verifiers → fix → spot-check → fix; EVERY round found something real. **FINAL E2E ON THE INSTALLED BUILD (2026-08-08 23:14, closed-loop emulator, all confirmed with all six guards passed): single-select all-short-labels ✓; N=2 one sealed request with Q1 digit + Q2 FREE TEXT verbatim ✓. The answer path is DONE — every answerable shape proven live; multiSelect free-text stays refused because the CLI itself commits the wrong option (refuted, not caution).**\n24\t\n25\t**2026-08-09 BATCH (commits 6a5a2e344 + 2d33f7491 + bd80b26a7, build 31330145092):** TWO live failures same day. (1) \"This desktop is too old\" on a 4-question prompt with a multiSelect item = hasUnprovenAnswerShape upfront refusal → pty-proved the shape (tmp/pty-proof-msel/PROOF.md, 11 runs incl. mixed freetext+multi both directions and zero-toggle): N>1 multiSelect group = toggle digits then \\x1b[C at ANY position (advance mid-prompt, review-screen landing on last), NEVER \\r inside a multiSelect group (\\r toggles the caret row silently — the old \"REFUTED\" verdict was only the N=1 tail pair \\x1b[C+\\r); free-text digit is the answering question's OWN options.length+1. Shape enabled end-to-end (multiselect_many, multiSelectManyBytesProven on 2.1.226 only); NO phone APK change (phone trusts answerable; watch still refuses all multiSelect by its own UI scope). Empty multiSelect is DRIVABLE but the CLI silently DROPS the question from the tool_result → user chose boundary refusal w/ explanatory 400 (empty_selection) over confirmed-with-silent-omission. (2) \"Unconfirmed - accepted the write but did not confirm\" killing free-text answers = guard-4 permission_axis KEPT veto power on weak same_prompt keystrokes (the text+\\r tail) and vetoed 2/2 mid-write (latch overwritten by unrelated hook events while the picker was verifiably up), aborting with the editor half-open → guard-4 now abstains on EVERY expectation form, never fails; it is ledger evidence only. Review round (Opus+Sol) also caught: attempt-wide guard evidence was last-keystroke-only (mergeAttemptEvidence: union abstains / intersect passes / AND raw readings — an abstain that permitted byte 1 can no longer vanish from ledger/audit/replay); guard-5 clip-contradiction check was disarmed on multiSelect items (no freeTextOption → verifyFreeTextRow never ran → bottom-clipped multi accepted) — fixed w/ detection-only `[ ] Type something` needle (multiSelectFreeTextRowDetectLabels, never pressable); digit addressability folded upfront; guard_failed log now carries full per-guard snapshot+expectation. 251 tests, 146 markers.\n26\t\n27\t**2026-08-09 LATE BATCH 2 (fork c1d873def build 31335480145 INSTALLED; companion 15ebcf8+1dc854e, both APKs sideloaded):** USER RULE LOCKED: any terminal question answerable from phone AND watch; ZERO upfront blockers without per-blocker user approval (currently approved: ONLY the empty-multiSelect refusal). Watch \"desktop bridge wouldn't allow\" RCA = the same N=4 multiSelect question hitting old SHAPE-UNPROVEN-UPFRONT (watch copy for capability_missing) — NOT a watch bug; but watch could not express multiselect at all (WearProtocol WatchAnswerItem had only Select). WATCH PARITY SHIPPED: WatchAnswerItem multiselect+freetext branches (lockstep wire, loud skew errors), checkbox rows (Done disabled at 0 ticked), RemoteInput free text (byte-for-byte, cancel = absent bundle), Answerability/watchCannotExpress shape gates DELETED, biometric ceremony DROPPED for answers AND messages (user-approved; bridge still requires confirmedBiometric=true on wire so clients send true always — it means \"deliberate send\" now). Round-2 review BLOCKER: WatchBridge intentShapeError still rejected confirmedBiometric=true → would have killed 100% of watch free text locally; + trim() exact-text violation. OBSERVABILITY: every sealed refusal, served question detail (granted+answerable+reason), answer intake, hello grants, picker-contract boot status now in host-service.log — read path was totally dark (RCA took an hour that should be one grep). adb ports ROTATE per wireless-debugging session — always re-ask user, verify device identity via getprop ro.product.model before install (user's port labels were swapped). OPEN: phone Send button doesn't mirror the ≥1-ticked rule (relies on bridge 400); watch E2E of multiselect answer not yet run post-desktop-install.\n28\t\n29\t**2026-08-10 FINAL E2E ON INSTALLED 1.20.0 (nightly had merged upstream v1.20.0 on top of all 08-09 work — verify tag ancestry via merge-commit parents, is-ancestor flaked once):** emulator closed-loop N=3 mixed (select+multiselect+freetext) ONE sealed request → confirmed, all six guards, abstained []; answers verbatim in the live AskUserQuestion result (Bravo / Mone+Mthree, Mtwo absent / free text exact). Empty multiselect → sealed 400 bad_request answers.1.optionIndexes too_small, visible via the new \"sealed refusal\" log line. PHYSICAL WATCH multiselect → answer_attempts surface=\"watch\" status=confirmed all six guards. Boot line picker_contract.status installed=proven=2.1.226 mismatch:false. NOT yet live-tested: watch free-text dictation (same relay path, code-reviewed + unit-tested only). closed_loop3.py = the reusable mixed-shape harness.\n30\t\n31\t**PHONE-PROTOCOL EMULATOR (keep using this):** `tmp/phone-emu/emu.ts` (bun) — imports the bridge's OWN crypto.ts, uses the real device key (NOT in host.db — plaintext at ~/.superset/companion/devices/<keyRef>.key.json), auto-handles Cloudflare Access JWT (service token → CF_Authorization cookie → replay as Cf-Access-Jwt-Assertion header — Access IS enforced on loopback), mandatory hello-before-anything (negotiated protocol byte bound into AADs). Commands: ping/tree/question/answer/freetext/status/replay/raw; `tmp/phone-emu/closed_loop.py` = arm-in-background-then-AskUserQuestion self-test. CLOSED-LOOP E2E PASSED: emulator answered a live AskUserQuestion in ~10s, ALL SIX guards passed, answer typed into the terminal, retract fired. This replaces poking the physical phone for every fix iteration.\n32\t\n33\tRelated: [[superset-companion-planning]], [[companion-durability-moved-to-hostdb]], [[companion-verification-recipes-and-traps]].\n34\t"}]},"uuid":"3911ab9e-f574-4e2c-9c3d-bea106160e07","timestamp":"2026-08-11T00:09:06.972Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\khair\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\memory\\project_companion_guard5_answer_path_fix.md","content":"---\nname: companion-guard5-answer-path-fix\ndescription: \"GUARD5 answer-path overhaul 2026-08-08: why every phone answer was refused, the 8-commit fix batch, the pty-proven 2.1.226 picker contract, and what is still refused by design\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91\n  modified: 2026-08-10T14:53:30.750Z\n---\n\n**Shipped 2026-08-08** (fork commits `10be67f65..d8eaa299a`, 8 commits pushed to main, build 31260063144 dispatched; rebuilds desktop-v1.19.0 in place). Root cause of \"The desktop refused: the question wasn't safely on screen\" on EVERY phone answer: guard 5's band check assumed option rows are adjacent lines, but real pickers render wrapped descriptions between rows (4 rows span 9-11 lines). Second barrier: 8-char label floor refused short labels (\"Skip\") upstream documents as the normal shape. Third: free-text row label drifted \"Other\"→\"Type something.\" (2.1.220→2.1.226). Lifetime answer_attempts before fix: 0 confirmed.\n\n**The fix shape (all in packages/host-service/src/companion/):** picker-block invariant — ascending line-anchored digit rows, each inter-row gap explained by the option-above's description ACTUALLY matched on screen (longest-matched-prefix budget, binary search over includes; never capture-claimed length), display-cell width vs screen-derived cols, memoised exhaustive placement search (digits repeat across N-question blocks; greedy strands rows). Evidence tiers: pressed row strong (label floor OR own description strictly in its own region — next row's line excluded), others digit-consistent, ≥1 strong option row at the accepted placement (enforced ONLY in rowsFormPickerBlock's sawStrongRow — a from:0 pre-check degenerated under the region clamp into a partial-write hazard on multiSelect: toggles written, submit refused). Free-text row: exact raw-line end-bounded match (no squash/case-fold — impostor options \"TYPE SOMETHING.\" must refuse), two-candidates=refuse, bound into the accepted placement. `PICKER_CONTRACTS` versioned map owns bytes+copy per CLI build; producer AND validator share `provenFreeTextRowLabel()` (they diverged once → validateCapture rejected EVERY normal capture at ingestion — the label is used in the capture cross-check, so the sink and store must derive from one constant).\n\n**Pty-proven on claude-code@2.1.226** (11 live pickers, tool_result ground truth; harness tmp/refusal-2026-08-08/pty_canary_node.mjs — MUST run under node, node-pty dies under Bun ERR_SOCKET_CLOSED): single-select ONE bare digit selects+submits; free-text = [digit N+1, text, \\r] (digit opens inline editor — a \"focused-not-open\" scare was an under-determined screen read; typed tool_result is the only ground truth); multiSelect: digits/space toggle, ENTER TOGGLES-NOT-SUBMITS, \\x1b[C opens a review screen then \\r submits; multiSelect DOES render free-text row \"Type something\" (no period) + chat row (old !multiSelect folklore wrong); \"Chat about this\" at N+2 in all pickers, sentinel __chat__, digits 1..N unshifted; N-question numbering restarts per question. TUI emits ESC[nC instead of spaces — naive ANSI strip breaks needles; replay through @xterm/headless.\n\n**Still refused by design (not bugs):** free-text on N>1 prompts (59% of traffic — biggest open UX gap, needs driven editor proof), multiSelect free-text, option indices >9, clipped-viewport (picker taller than window → row_absent). Runtime drift detector (proven-version.ts) reports installed-CLI-vs-PROVEN_AGAINST on companion.gate — memoise ONLY successful reads (a cached null suppressed the warning forever). Open follow-ups: guard-4 permission_axis flaky latch, stale armed fence row Jg3tdkW8zw2lcMBkiKyyqw w/ missing transcript, be9a2256e's commit message falsely claims free-text contract known-wrong (retracted in 9a3ff0c13).\n\n**Process notes that paid:** live E2E before shipping — stage-1 dry-run harness (tmp/refusal-2026-08-08/e2e_answer_harness.ts) runs real matcher+encoder against the live viewport via terminal.snapshot/writeInput tRPC (manifest Bearer; response is superjson: result.data.json); it caught that the user's \"same chat\" was a DIFFERENT terminal (always resolve the pending tool_use, never trust a stale terminal id). Review cycle: 2 reviewers → fix → 2 fresh verifiers → fix → spot-check found NEW bugs every round incl. a BLOCKER introduced BY a fix; ~28 verified findings total. Answer path proven live twice (option A raw write; option B via full patched-guard harness).\n\n**SESSION-REHELLO (same day, after reinstall): the \"This desktop can't take that — answer at the desk\" error at question-OPEN is a DIFFERENT bug** — bridge sessions are in-memory; desktop restart wipes them; the phone cached its wireSession for the 1h TTL and never re-helloed (§6.3 was specced but unimplemented), so every gated route 501'd capability_unsupported for up to an hour after EVERY restart while ungated tree/heartbeat kept the app looking healthy. Fixed phone-side `9b9aae2`+`a6dcd98` (discard on restart-detect + on capability 501; sessions BOUND to bridge lifetime via first beat — only a session predating the observed lifetime is stale; identity-scoped compare-and-set invalidation under one lock so a delayed S0 error can't clear fresh S1) — both APKs sideloaded 2026-08-08 evening. Fork hardening `af4994acd` (pushed, ships next build): dead session now gets distinct sealed 409 session_expired instead of masquerading as 501. LIVE RESTART TEST STILL PENDING: next Superset restart → open phone app → answer a question (one retry allowed in the rare hello-vs-first-beat race).\n\n**COMPLETION BATCH (same day, evening — 6 more commits 2de601b67..9c42a38c2 pushed, build 31278552490):** (FREETEXT-N2-PROVEN) free-text ENABLED on N>1 all-single-select prompts — pty-proven per-question groups [digit N+1, text, \\r] which ADVANCE (free-text on last question = two consecutive \\r; final \\r on review screen submits); multiSelect free-text REFUTED not just unproven (terminal swallows the text and commits the caret row — proven wrong-answer), multiSelect-inside-N>1 REFUTED (\\x1b[C means \"Next\" there → selects a question never asked) — both stay refused forever unless upstream changes. (GUARD5-CLIPPED-VIEWPORT) prefix/suffix clips accepted when the clipped edge is affirmatively explained (endsWith-positional suffix match — `includes` was a proven forgery hole; clip needle floor = 12) and the pressed row is visible+strong. (GUARD4-ABSTAIN) permission_axis abstains ONLY on strong item_picker keystrokes when all load-bearing guards passed (weak same_prompt keystrokes keep refusal — matchPromptStillOnScreen matches a picker-GONE echo); abstain is a distinct outcome threaded through ledger/audit/wire; replay derives it (null = cannot say). (PUSH-ORPHAN-GONE/STALE-VERDICT) orphan fence verdict tri-state resolved|unresolved|gone (gone = projects root AND slug dir stat + transcript ENOENT → retire without buzz) with generation-checked async currency (adoption/deadline race was losing live notifications). ~40 verified review findings total across the day, every serious one executed not argued. Review cadence that worked: 2 reviewers → fix → 2 fresh verifiers → fix → spot-check → fix; EVERY round found something real. **FINAL E2E ON THE INSTALLED BUILD (2026-08-08 23:14, closed-loop emulator, all confirmed with all six guards passed): single-select all-short-labels ✓; N=2 one sealed request with Q1 digit + Q2 FREE TEXT verbatim ✓. The answer path is DONE — every answerable shape proven live; multiSelect free-text stays refused because the CLI itself commits the wrong option (refuted, not caution).**\n\n**2026-08-09 BATCH (commits 6a5a2e344 + 2d33f7491 + bd80b26a7, build 31330145092):** TWO live failures same day. (1) \"This desktop is too old\" on a 4-question prompt with a multiSelect item = hasUnprovenAnswerShape upfront refusal → pty-proved the shape (tmp/pty-proof-msel/PROOF.md, 11 runs incl. mixed freetext+multi both directions and zero-toggle): N>1 multiSelect group = toggle digits then \\x1b[C at ANY position (advance mid-prompt, review-screen landing on last), NEVER \\r inside a multiSelect group (\\r toggles the caret row silently — the old \"REFUTED\" verdict was only the N=1 tail pair \\x1b[C+\\r); free-text digit is the answering question's OWN options.length+1. Shape enabled end-to-end (multiselect_many, multiSelectManyBytesProven on 2.1.226 only); NO phone APK change (phone trusts answerable; watch still refuses all multiSelect by its own UI scope). Empty multiSelect is DRIVABLE but the CLI silently DROPS the question from the tool_result → user chose boundary refusal w/ explanatory 400 (empty_selection) over confirmed-with-silent-omission. (2) \"Unconfirmed - accepted the write but did not confirm\" killing free-text answers = guard-4 permission_axis KEPT veto power on weak same_prompt keystrokes (the text+\\r tail) and vetoed 2/2 mid-write (latch overwritten by unrelated hook events while the picker was verifiably up), aborting with the editor half-open → guard-4 now abstains on EVERY expectation form, never fails; it is ledger evidence only. Review round (Opus+Sol) also caught: attempt-wide guard evidence was last-keystroke-only (mergeAttemptEvidence: union abstains / intersect passes / AND raw readings — an abstain that permitted byte 1 can no longer vanish from ledger/audit/replay); guard-5 clip-contradiction check was disarmed on multiSelect items (no freeTextOption → verifyFreeTextRow never ran → bottom-clipped multi accepted) — fixed w/ detection-only `[ ] Type something` needle (multiSelectFreeTextRowDetectLabels, never pressable); digit addressability folded upfront; guard_failed log now carries full per-guard snapshot+expectation. 251 tests, 146 markers.\n\n**2026-08-09 LATE BATCH 2 (fork c1d873def build 31335480145 INSTALLED; companion 15ebcf8+1dc854e, both APKs sideloaded):** USER RULE LOCKED: any terminal question answerable from phone AND watch; ZERO upfront blockers without per-blocker user approval (currently approved: ONLY the empty-multiSelect refusal). Watch \"desktop bridge wouldn't allow\" RCA = the same N=4 multiSelect question hitting old SHAPE-UNPROVEN-UPFRONT (watch copy for capability_missing) — NOT a watch bug; but watch could not express multiselect at all (WearProtocol WatchAnswerItem had only Select). WATCH PARITY SHIPPED: WatchAnswerItem multiselect+freetext branches (lockstep wire, loud skew errors), checkbox rows (Done disabled at 0 ticked), RemoteInput free text (byte-for-byte, cancel = absent bundle), Answerability/watchCannotExpress shape gates DELETED, biometric ceremony DROPPED for answers AND messages (user-approved; bridge still requires confirmedBiometric=true on wire so clients send true always — it means \"deliberate send\" now). Round-2 review BLOCKER: WatchBridge intentShapeError still rejected confirmedBiometric=true → would have killed 100% of watch free text locally; + trim() exact-text violation. OBSERVABILITY: every sealed refusal, served question detail (granted+answerable+reason), answer intake, hello grants, picker-contract boot status now in host-service.log — read path was totally dark (RCA took an hour that should be one grep). adb ports ROTATE per wireless-debugging session — always re-ask user, verify device identity via getprop ro.product.model before install (user's port labels were swapped). OPEN: phone Send button doesn't mirror the ≥1-ticked rule (relies on bridge 400); watch E2E of multiselect answer not yet run post-desktop-install.\n\n**2026-08-10 FINAL E2E ON INSTALLED 1.20.0 (nightly had merged upstream v1.20.0 on top of all 08-09 work — verify tag ancestry via merge-commit parents, is-ancestor flaked once):** emulator closed-loop N=3 mixed (select+multiselect+freetext) ONE sealed request → confirmed, all six guards, abstained []; answers verbatim in the live AskUserQuestion result (Bravo / Mone+Mthree, Mtwo absent / free text exact). Empty multiselect → sealed 400 bad_request answers.1.optionIndexes too_small, visible via the new \"sealed refusal\" log line. PHYSICAL WATCH multiselect → answer_attempts surface=\"watch\" status=confirmed all six guards. Boot line picker_contract.status installed=proven=2.1.226 mismatch:false. NOT yet live-tested: watch free-text dictation (same relay path, code-reviewed + unit-tested only). closed_loop3.py = the reusable mixed-shape harness.\n\n**PHONE-PROTOCOL EMULATOR (keep using this):** `tmp/phone-emu/emu.ts` (bun) — imports the bridge's OWN crypto.ts, uses the real device key (NOT in host.db — plaintext at ~/.superset/companion/devices/<keyRef>.key.json), auto-handles Cloudflare Access JWT (service token → CF_Authorization cookie → replay as Cf-Access-Jwt-Assertion header — Access IS enforced on loopback), mandatory hello-before-anything (negotiated protocol byte bound into AADs). Commands: ping/tree/question/answer/freetext/status/replay/raw; `tmp/phone-emu/closed_loop.py` = arm-in-background-then-AskUserQuestion self-test. CLOSED-LOOP E2E PASSED: emulator answered a live AskUserQuestion in ~10s, ALL SIX guards passed, answer typed into the terminal, retract fired. This replaces poking the physical phone for every fix iteration.\n\nRelated: [[superset-companion-planning]], [[companion-durability-moved-to-hostdb]], [[companion-verification-recipes-and-traps]].\n","numLines":34,"startLine":1,"totalLines":34}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"53a9c876-b1d0-44c5-9c24-80e83af60f76","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.226","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"3911ab9e-f574-4e2c-9c3d-bea106160e07","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"task_reminder","content":[{"id":"1","subject":"Answer the open question with option one","description":"Use the installed companion emulator against the still-open question and submit the user's requested first option, recording the live result.","activeForm":"Answering the open question","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"2","subject":"Remove all answer guards","description":"Change the desktop bridge so no transcript, screen, session, binding, permission-axis, marker, or similar runtime guard can refuse a remotely expressible answer. Preserve only API shape validation needed to encode the selected answer; follow the user's directive that any question visible in the terminal must remain answerable from phone/watch.","activeForm":"Removing all answer guards","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"3","subject":"Verify and ship the guardless path","description":"Add/adjust tests for locked or off-screen desktop operation, run required scoped validation and reviews, commit directly to main, push, and start the full GitHub build for installation later.","activeForm":"Verifying and shipping the guardless path","status":"in_progress","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"4","subject":"Acknowledge companion PTY writes","description":"Add a daemon-backed acknowledged raw-input operation so companion answer writes report success only after session.pty.write succeeds; propagate zero/partial failures honestly and test missing/exited/write-error cases.","activeForm":"Acknowledging companion PTY writes","owner":"pty-ack","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[],"metadata":{"verification":"Daemon/protocol unit tests 28/28; companion suite 263/263; REFERR-GATE clean; pty-daemon bundle builds. Host build/typecheck reach only merged v1.20 dependency/pre-existing errors, zero new acknowledgment diagnostics. DaemonClient integration test added for Linux; local Windows cannot bind Unix .sock (EACCES)."}},{"id":"5","subject":"Make confirmed outcome durable","description":"Stop swallowing confirmed ledger transition failures. Return confirmed only after the durable transition commits; bytes-written persistence failure must become fenced honest unconfirmed behavior without duplicate execution.","activeForm":"Making confirmed outcomes durable","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"6","subject":"Repair transcript unreadable caching","description":"Do not cache transient unreadable transcript verdicts so a later successful read can positively settle a desk-answered question.","activeForm":"Repairing transcript reconciliation caching","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[],"metadata":{"verification":"14 question-lifecycle tests pass; unchanged transcript is rescanned after unreadable and resolves on second pass."}},{"id":"7","subject":"Expose every pending question","description":"Ensure paired phone/watch can discover and fetch every pending captured question regardless of missing session/capability or sidebar curation, while preserving authentication and semantic validation.","activeForm":"Exposing every pending question","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[],"metadata":{"verification":"68 curation/session tests pass. Baseline no-grant tree exposes pending refs through curated-off workspace/project; /v1/question is session/capability ungated but remains paired/sealed/schema validated."}},{"id":"8","subject":"Contain partial-write audit failures","description":"After a durable partial-write unconfirmed outcome, catch/log audit sink failure and return unconfirmed rather than throwing.","activeForm":"Containing partial-write audit failures","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"9","subject":"Restore guardless type safety","description":"Resolve new callback/result diagnostics from synchronous injection and update lease mocks to the current shape without reintroducing guards.","activeForm":"Restoring guardless type safety","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[],"metadata":{"verification":"Host-service typecheck now reports only the two pre-existing terminal.ts diagnostics; 5 guardless tests pass."}},{"id":"10","subject":"Fence ambiguous acknowledged-write failures","description":"Differentiate daemon/PTTY outcomes that provably wrote zero bytes from timeout/disconnect outcomes where the first byte may have landed; ambiguous first-write outcomes must return durable unconfirmed and retain a duplicate fence, never invite retry as zero-write failed.","activeForm":"Fencing ambiguous write outcomes","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"11","subject":"Protect reconcile settlement races","description":"Re-check pending state immediately before transcript reconciliation settles a question, preserving phone provenance/stale terminal state if another path settled it during awaits.","activeForm":"Protecting reconcile settlement races","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"12","subject":"Align heartbeat pending-question counts","description":"Make heartbeat status counts apply the same curated-workspace exception as tree projection for terminals carrying a pending captured question.","activeForm":"Aligning heartbeat question counts","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"13","subject":"Migrate detached PTY protocol safely","description":"Keep v2 ordinary terminal adoption compatible while requiring v3 before acknowledged companion writes; bump daemon package version and verify old-daemon adoption/update detection rather than retaining an unreachable unknown instance.","activeForm":"Migrating detached PTY protocol","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]}],"itemCount":13},"type":"attachment","uuid":"9820f113-8953-4484-a327-93105765efff","timestamp":"2026-08-11T00:09:07.078Z","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd"