adback, honest `not_written` vs `unknown`, audit-failure containment, and positive-only transcript settlement. Cleanup commit `7e0d25f3c` removed the retired ~4.6k-line guard/matcher/test stack while preserving `/v1/message` picker protections; Opus validation: REFERR clean, 200 companion tests + 11 fault probes passed, only accepted TS2554 debt; `/code-review low` found nothing. Both pushed to main. Full Windows ARM64 publish build `31443284669` succeeded on sha `7e0d25f3c0ecec91324b5302b265674269800cac`; prior build `31437447650` also succeeded on `ec83cf8e4`. Installer NOT installed yet—must wait for the user's explicit exact-time authorization because it closes Superset/session. Post-install verification still required: real phone/watch answer, renderer hidden/display off/Windows locked-login boundary, detached v2→v3 migration, acknowledgment+ledger logs, and no `guard_failed` answer outcome. Never log free-text bodies, keys, tokens, or transcript content.\n\nRelated: [[superset-companion-planning]], [[companion-durability-moved-to-hostdb]], [[companion-verification-recipes-and-traps]].","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":5,"oldLines":7,"newStart":5,"newLines":7,"lines":["   node_type: memory","   type: project","   originSessionId: 41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","-  modified: 2026-08-11T00:09:29.590Z","+  modified: 2026-08-11T00:10:14.446Z"," ---"," "," **Shipped 2026-08-08** (fork commits `10be67f65..d8eaa299a`, 8 commits pushed to main, build 31260063144 dispatched; rebuilds desktop-v1.19.0 in place). Root cause of \"The desktop refused: the question wasn't safely on screen\" on EVERY phone answer: guard 5's band check assumed option rows are adjacent lines, but real pickers render wrapped descriptions between rows (4 rows span 9-11 lines). Second barrier: 8-char label floor refused short labels (\"Skip\") upstream documents as the normal shape. Third: free-text row label drifted \"Other\"→\"Type something.\" (2.1.220→2.1.226). Lifetime answer_attempts before fix: 0 confirmed."]},{"oldStart":30,"oldLines":4,"newStart":30,"newLines":6,"lines":[" "," **PHONE-PROTOCOL EMULATOR (keep using this):** `tmp/phone-emu/emu.ts` (bun) — imports the bridge's OWN crypto.ts, uses the real device key (NOT in host.db — plaintext at ~/.superset/companion/devices/<keyRef>.key.json), auto-handles Cloudflare Access JWT (service token → CF_Authorization cookie → replay as Cf-Access-Jwt-Assertion header — Access IS enforced on loopback), mandatory hello-before-anything (negotiated protocol byte bound into AADs). Commands: ping/tree/question/answer/freetext/status/replay/raw; `tmp/phone-emu/closed_loop.py` = arm-in-background-then-AskUserQuestion self-test. CLOSED-LOOP E2E PASSED: emulator answered a live AskUserQuestion in ~10s, ALL SIX guards passed, answer typed into the terminal, retract fired. This replaces poking the physical phone for every fix iteration."," ","+**2026-08-10/11 ANSWER-GUARDLESS FINAL SHIP:** user locked the whole-UX contract: any captured pending Claude question with a real terminal target must remain discoverable and answerable from phone/watch regardless of transcript readability/state, live screen/render state, renderer availability, Windows display/lock/login state, mutable agent binding, permission axis, AskUser marker, read-side liveness, or negotiated answer capability/session state. Security/API boundaries retained: pairing/authenticated device, Cloudflare Access, sealed AES-GCM transport, nonce replay protection, schemas/semantic shape validation, exact current question+fingerprint at the last synchronous pre-write point, answer-wide lease, terminal lock, durable request claim/fence, actual PTY failures, and protocol-0 read-only. Commit `ec83cf8e4` removed every production answer guard, made pending questions pierce curation and capability hiding, added protocol-v3 correlated daemon-side `pty.write` acknowledgments, v2 whole-sequence legacy fallback with durable `unconfirmed` fencing, detached-session adoption before lease/lock, durable outcome write+readback, honest `not_written` vs `unknown`, audit-failure containment, and positive-only transcript settlement. Cleanup commit `7e0d25f3c` removed the retired ~4.6k-line guard/matcher/test stack while preserving `/v1/message` picker protections; Opus validation: REFERR clean, 200 companion tests + 11 fault probes passed, only accepted TS2554 debt; `/code-review low` found nothing. Both pushed to main. Full Windows ARM64 publish build `31443284669` succeeded on sha `7e0d25f3c0ecec91324b5302b265674269800cac`; prior build `31437447650` also succeeded on `ec83cf8e4`. Installer NOT installed yet—must wait for the user's explicit exact-time authorization because it closes Superset/session. Post-install verification still required: real phone/watch answer, renderer hidden/display off/Windows locked-login boundary, detached v2→v3 migration, acknowledgment+ledger logs, and no `guard_failed` answer outcome. Never log free-text bodies, keys, tokens, or transcript content.","+"," Related: [[superset-companion-planning]], [[companion-durability-moved-to-hostdb]], [[companion-verification-recipes-and-traps]]."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"memdirStamped":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b6576a4d-f5cd-4ee5-9598-9daacd19602d","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.226","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
