{"parentUuid":"3e606625-1c22-4cdb-9b34-1008fa5d6333","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"C:\\Users\\khair\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\memory\\project_companion_guard5_answer_path_fix.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\khair\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\memory\\project_companion_guard5_answer_path_fix.md","content":"---\nname: companion-guard5-answer-path-fix\ndescription: \"Companion answer history through 2026-08-11: the retired guard stack, guardless answer contract, acknowledged PTY writes, durable outcomes, and shipped build evidence\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91\n  modified: 2026-08-11T00:10:14.446Z\n---\n\n**Shipped 2026-08-08** (fork commits `10be67f65..d8eaa299a`, 8 commits pushed to main, build 31260063144 dispatched; rebuilds desktop-v1.19.0 in place). Root cause of \"The desktop refused: the question wasn't safely on screen\" on EVERY phone answer: guard 5's band check assumed option rows are adjacent lines, but real pickers render wrapped descriptions between rows (4 rows span 9-11 lines). Second barrier: 8-char label floor refused short labels (\"Skip\") upstream documents as the normal shape. Third: free-text row label drifted \"Other\"→\"Type something.\" (2.1.220→2.1.226). Lifetime answer_attempts before fix: 0 confirmed.\n\n**The fix shape (all in packages/host-service/src/companion/):** picker-block invariant — ascending line-anchored digit rows, each inter-row gap explained by the option-above's description ACTUALLY matched on screen (longest-matched-prefix budget, binary search over includes; never capture-claimed length), display-cell width vs screen-derived cols, memoised exhaustive placement search (digits repeat across N-question blocks; greedy strands rows). Evidence tiers: pressed row strong (label floor OR own description strictly in its own region — next row's line excluded), others digit-consistent, ≥1 strong option row at the accepted placement (enforced ONLY in rowsFormPickerBlock's sawStrongRow — a from:0 pre-check degenerated under the region clamp into a partial-write hazard on multiSelect: toggles written, submit refused). Free-text row: exact raw-line end-bounded match (no squash/case-fold — impostor options \"TYPE SOMETHING.\" must refuse), two-candidates=refuse, bound into the accepted placement. `PICKER_CONTRACTS` versioned map owns bytes+copy per CLI build; producer AND validator share `provenFreeTextRowLabel()` (they diverged once → validateCapture rejected EVERY normal capture at ingestion — the label is used in the capture cross-check, so the sink and store must derive from one constant).\n\n**Pty-proven on claude-code@2.1.226** (11 live pickers, tool_result ground truth; harness tmp/refusal-2026-08-08/pty_canary_node.mjs — MUST run under node, node-pty dies under Bun ERR_SOCKET_CLOSED): single-select ONE bare digit selects+submits; free-text = [digit N+1, text, \\r] (digit opens inline editor — a \"focused-not-open\" scare was an under-determined screen read; typed tool_result is the only ground truth); multiSelect: digits/space toggle, ENTER TOGGLES-NOT-SUBMITS, \\x1b[C opens a review screen then \\r submits; multiSelect DOES render free-text row \"Type something\" (no period) + chat row (old !multiSelect folklore wrong); \"Chat about this\" at N+2 in all pickers, sentinel __chat__, digits 1..N unshifted; N-question numbering restarts per question. TUI emits ESC[nC instead of spaces — naive ANSI strip breaks needles; replay through @xterm/headless.\n\n**Still refused by design (not bugs):** free-text on N>1 prompts (59% of traffic — biggest open UX gap, needs driven editor proof), multiSelect free-text, option indices >9, clipped-viewport (picker taller than window → row_absent). Runtime drift detector (proven-version.ts) reports installed-CLI-vs-PROVEN_AGAINST on companion.gate — memoise ONLY successful reads (a cached null suppressed the warning forever). Open follow-ups: guard-4 permission_axis flaky latch, stale armed fence row Jg3tdkW8zw2lcMBkiKyyqw w/ missing transcript, be9a2256e's commit message falsely claims free-text contract known-wrong (retracted in 9a3ff0c13).\n\n**Process notes that paid:** live E2E before shipping — stage-1 dry-run harness (tmp/refusal-2026-08-08/e2e_answer_harness.ts) runs real matcher+encoder against the live viewport via terminal.snapshot/writeInput tRPC (manifest Bearer; response is superjson: result.data.json); it caught that the user's \"same chat\" was a DIFFERENT terminal (always resolve the pending tool_use, never trust a stale terminal id). Review cycle: 2 reviewers → fix → 2 fresh verifiers → fix → spot-check found NEW bugs every round incl. a BLOCKER introduced BY a fix; ~28 verified findings total. Answer path proven live twice (option A raw write; option B via full patched-guard harness).\n\n**SESSION-REHELLO (same day, after reinstall): the \"This desktop can't take that — answer at the desk\" error at question-OPEN is a DIFFERENT bug** — bridge sessions are in-memory; desktop restart wipes them; the phone cached its wireSession for the 1h TTL and never re-helloed (§6.3 was specced but unimplemented), so every gated route 501'd capability_unsupported for up to an hour after EVERY restart while ungated tree/heartbeat kept the app looking healthy. Fixed phone-side `9b9aae2`+`a6dcd98` (discard on restart-detect + on capability 501; sessions BOUND to bridge lifetime via first beat — only a session predating the observed lifetime is stale; identity-scoped compare-and-set invalidation under one lock so a delayed S0 error can't clear fresh S1) — both APKs sideloaded 2026-08-08 evening. Fork hardening `af4994acd` (pushed, ships next build): dead session now gets distinct sealed 409 session_expired instead of masquerading as 501. LIVE RESTART TEST STILL PENDING: next Superset restart → open phone app → answer a question (one retry allowed in the rare hello-vs-first-beat race).\n\n**COMPLETION BATCH (same day, evening — 6 more commits 2de601b67..9c42a38c2 pushed, build 31278552490):** (FREETEXT-N2-PROVEN) free-text ENABLED on N>1 all-single-select prompts — pty-proven per-question groups [digit N+1, text, \\r] which ADVANCE (free-text on last question = two consecutive \\r; final \\r on review screen submits); multiSelect free-text REFUTED not just unproven (terminal swallows the text and commits the caret row — proven wrong-answer), multiSelect-inside-N>1 REFUTED (\\x1b[C means \"Next\" there → selects a question never asked) — both stay refused forever unless upstream changes. (GUARD5-CLIPPED-VIEWPORT) prefix/suffix clips accepted when the clipped edge is affirmatively explained (endsWith-positional suffix match — `includes` was a proven forgery hole; clip needle floor = 12) and the pressed row is visible+strong. (GUARD4-ABSTAIN) permission_axis abstains ONLY on strong item_picker keystrokes when all load-bearing guards passed (weak same_prompt keystrokes keep refusal — matchPromptStillOnScreen matches a picker-GONE echo); abstain is a distinct outcome threaded through ledger/audit/wire; replay derives it (null = cannot say). (PUSH-ORPHAN-GONE/STALE-VERDICT) orphan fence verdict tri-state resolved|unresolved|gone (gone = projects root AND slug dir stat + transcript ENOENT → retire without buzz) with generation-checked async currency (adoption/deadline race was losing live notifications). ~40 verified review findings total across the day, every serious one executed not argued. Review cadence that worked: 2 reviewers → fix → 2 fresh verifiers → fix → spot-check → fix; EVERY round found something real. **FINAL E2E ON THE INSTALLED BUILD (2026-08-08 23:14, closed-loop emulator, all confirmed with all six guards passed): single-select all-short-labels ✓; N=2 one sealed request with Q1 digit + Q2 FREE TEXT verbatim ✓. The answer path is DONE — every answerable shape proven live; multiSelect free-text stays refused because the CLI itself commits the wrong option (refuted, not caution).**\n\n**2026-08-09 BATCH (commits 6a5a2e344 + 2d33f7491 + bd80b26a7, build 31330145092):** TWO live failures same day. (1) \"This desktop is too old\" on a 4-question prompt with a multiSelect item = hasUnprovenAnswerShape upfront refusal → pty-proved the shape (tmp/pty-proof-msel/PROOF.md, 11 runs incl. mixed freetext+multi both directions and zero-toggle): N>1 multiSelect group = toggle digits then \\x1b[C at ANY position (advance mid-prompt, review-screen landing on last), NEVER \\r inside a multiSelect group (\\r toggles the caret row silently — the old \"REFUTED\" verdict was only the N=1 tail pair \\x1b[C+\\r); free-text digit is the answering question's OWN options.length+1. Shape enabled end-to-end (multiselect_many, multiSelectManyBytesProven on 2.1.226 only); NO phone APK change (phone trusts answerable; watch still refuses all multiSelect by its own UI scope). Empty multiSelect is DRIVABLE but the CLI silently DROPS the question from the tool_result → user chose boundary refusal w/ explanatory 400 (empty_selection) over confirmed-with-silent-omission. (2) \"Unconfirmed - accepted the write but did not confirm\" killing free-text answers = guard-4 permission_axis KEPT veto power on weak same_prompt keystrokes (the text+\\r tail) and vetoed 2/2 mid-write (latch overwritten by unrelated hook events while the picker was verifiably up), aborting with the editor half-open → guard-4 now abstains on EVERY expectation form, never fails; it is ledger evidence only. Review round (Opus+Sol) also caught: attempt-wide guard evidence was last-keystroke-only (mergeAttemptEvidence: union abstains / intersect passes / AND raw readings — an abstain that permitted byte 1 can no longer vanish from ledger/audit/replay); guard-5 clip-contradiction check was disarmed on multiSelect items (no freeTextOption → verifyFreeTextRow never ran → bottom-clipped multi accepted) — fixed w/ detection-only `[ ] Type something` needle (multiSelectFreeTextRowDetectLabels, never pressable); digit addressability folded upfront; guard_failed log now carries full per-guard snapshot+expectation. 251 tests, 146 markers.\n\n**2026-08-09 LATE BATCH 2 (fork c1d873def build 31335480145 INSTALLED; companion 15ebcf8+1dc854e, both APKs sideloaded):** USER RULE LOCKED: any terminal question answerable from phone AND watch; ZERO upfront blockers without per-blocker user approval (currently approved: ONLY the empty-multiSelect refusal). Watch \"desktop bridge wouldn't allow\" RCA = the same N=4 multiSelect question hitting old SHAPE-UNPROVEN-UPFRONT (watch copy for capability_missing) — NOT a watch bug; but watch could not express multiselect at all (WearProtocol WatchAnswerItem had only Select). WATCH PARITY SHIPPED: WatchAnswerItem multiselect+freetext branches (lockstep wire, loud skew errors), checkbox rows (Done disabled at 0 ticked), RemoteInput free text (byte-for-byte, cancel = absent bundle), Answerability/watchCannotExpress shape gates DELETED, biometric ceremony DROPPED for answers AND messages (user-approved; bridge still requires confirmedBiometric=true on wire so clients send true always — it means \"deliberate send\" now). Round-2 review BLOCKER: WatchBridge intentShapeError still rejected confirmedBiometric=true → would have killed 100% of watch free text locally; + trim() exact-text violation. OBSERVABILITY: every sealed refusal, served question detail (granted+answerable+reason), answer intake, hello grants, picker-contract boot status now in host-service.log — read path was totally dark (RCA took an hour that should be one grep). adb ports ROTATE per wireless-debugging session — always re-ask user, verify device identity via getprop ro.product.model before install (user's port labels were swapped). OPEN: phone Send button doesn't mirror the ≥1-ticked rule (relies on bridge 400); watch E2E of multiselect answer not yet run post-desktop-install.\n\n**2026-08-10 FINAL E2E ON INSTALLED 1.20.0 (nightly had merged upstream v1.20.0 on top of all 08-09 work — verify tag ancestry via merge-commit parents, is-ancestor flaked once):** emulator closed-loop N=3 mixed (select+multiselect+freetext) ONE sealed request → confirmed, all six guards, abstained []; answers verbatim in the live AskUserQuestion result (Bravo / Mone+Mthree, Mtwo absent / free text exact). Empty multiselect → sealed 400 bad_request answers.1.optionIndexes too_small, visible via the new \"sealed refusal\" log line. PHYSICAL WATCH multiselect → answer_attempts surface=\"watch\" status=confirmed all six guards. Boot line picker_contract.status installed=proven=2.1.226 mismatch:false. NOT yet live-tested: watch free-text dictation (same relay path, code-reviewed + unit-tested only). closed_loop3.py = the reusable mixed-shape harness.\n\n**PHONE-PROTOCOL EMULATOR (keep using this):** `tmp/phone-emu/emu.ts` (bun) — imports the bridge's OWN crypto.ts, uses the real device key (NOT in host.db — plaintext at ~/.superset/companion/devices/<keyRef>.key.json), auto-handles Cloudflare Access JWT (service token → CF_Authorization cookie → replay as Cf-Access-Jwt-Assertion header — Access IS enforced on loopback), mandatory hello-before-anything (negotiated protocol byte bound into AADs). Commands: ping/tree/question/answer/freetext/status/replay/raw; `tmp/phone-emu/closed_loop.py` = arm-in-background-then-AskUserQuestion self-test. CLOSED-LOOP E2E PASSED: emulator answered a live AskUserQuestion in ~10s, ALL SIX guards passed, answer typed into the terminal, retract fired. This replaces poking the physical phone for every fix iteration.\n\n**2026-08-10/11 ANSWER-GUARDLESS FINAL SHIP:** user locked the whole-UX contract: any captured pending Claude question with a real terminal target must remain discoverable and answerable from phone/watch regardless of transcript readability/state, live screen/render state, renderer availability, Windows display/lock/login state, mutable agent binding, permission axis, AskUser marker, read-side liveness, or negotiated answer capability/session state. Security/API boundaries retained: pairing/authenticated device, Cloudflare Access, sealed AES-GCM transport, nonce replay protection, schemas/semantic shape validation, exact current question+fingerprint at the last synchronous pre-write point, answer-wide lease, terminal lock, durable request claim/fence, actual PTY failures, and protocol-0 read-only. Commit `ec83cf8e4` removed every production answer guard, made pending questions pierce curation and capability hiding, added protocol-v3 correlated daemon-side `pty.write` acknowledgments, v2 whole-sequence legacy fallback with durable `unconfirmed` fencing, detached-session adoption before lease/lock, durable outcome write+readback, honest `not_written` vs `unknown`, audit-failure containment, and positive-only transcript settlement. Cleanup commit `7e0d25f3c` removed the retired ~4.6k-line guard/matcher/test stack while preserving `/v1/message` picker protections; Opus validation: REFERR clean, 200 companion tests + 11 fault probes passed, only accepted TS2554 debt; `/code-review low` found nothing. Both pushed to main. Full Windows ARM64 publish build `31443284669` succeeded on sha `7e0d25f3c0ecec91324b5302b265674269800cac`; prior build `31437447650` also succeeded on `ec83cf8e4`. Installer NOT installed yet—must wait for the user's explicit exact-time authorization because it closes Superset/session. Post-install verification still required: real phone/watch answer, renderer hidden/display off/Windows locked-login boundary, detached v2→v3 migration, acknowledgment+ledger logs, and no `guard_failed` answer outcome. Never log free-text bodies, keys, tokens, or transcript content.\n\nRelated: [[superset-companion-planning]], [[companion-durability-moved-to-hostdb]], [[companion-verification-recipes-and-traps]].\n","numLines":36,"startLine":1,"totalLines":36}},"displayPath":"..\\..\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\memory\\project_companion_guard5_answer_path_fix.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"21fac81c-f46d-4a3d-943f-99da1c6d5df5","timestamp":"2026-08-12T01:48:19.193Z","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.226","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"21fac81c-f46d-4a3d-943f-99da1c6d5df5","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\4e98c32a-1d17-48da-bc15-302ae5043fea\\tasks\\bqi02cxlu.output","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\4e98c32a-1d17-48da-bc15-302ae5043fea\\tasks\\bqi02cxlu.output","content":"OK   apps/desktop (78s) — 0 dangerous (84 total diagnostics, debt allowed)\nFAIL packages/host-service (22s) — 1 ReferenceError-class diagnostic(s):\n::error::(REFERR-GATE) packages/host-service: src/companion/answer.ts(502,5): error TS2304: Cannot find name 'PickerScreenMatch'.\nOK   packages/shared (2s) — 0 dangerous (0 total diagnostics, debt allowed)\nOK   packages/local-db (2s) — 0 dangerous (0 total diagnostics, debt allowed)\nOK   packages/panes (2s) — 0 dangerous (0 total diagnostics, debt allowed)\nOK   packages/ui (5s) — 0 dangerous (1 total diagnostics, debt allowed)\nOK   packages/workspace-client (20s) — 0 dangerous (3 total diagnostics, debt allowed)\n::error::(REFERR-GATE) cannot-find-name diagnostics found — a bare identifier would throw ReferenceError in the shipped bundle. Fix before building.\n","numLines":10,"startLine":1,"totalLines":10}},"displayPath":"..\\..\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\4e98c32a-1d17-48da-bc15-302ae5043fea\\tasks\\bqi02cxlu.output"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"fb02113e-9d33-479b-a6e5-fdb62f2cbc48","timestamp":"2026-08-12T01:48:19.116Z","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.226","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
