{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-12T02:16:52.793Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<agent-message from=\"emulator-prep\">\nExact recommended orchestration after YOU create the redacted throwaway harness at `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\phone-emu\\closed_loop_safe.py`:\n\n1. Arm in the background (yes, this works; it polls while AskUser blocks):\n`uv run python \"C:/Users/khair/Code Projects/fork-superset-windows-arm64/tmp/phone-emu/closed_loop_safe.py\"`\nRun via Bash/PowerShell with `run_in_background:true` and a 420s timeout. The safe script should internally execute `bun run tmp/phone-emu/emu-safe.ts ...` from repo root and print only phase/result metadata.\n\n2. Immediately issue ONE real AskUserQuestion in this same main terminal/session with exactly one single-select question and two options:\n- header: `E2E check`\n- question: `Which test result should the companion submit?`\n- multiSelect: `false`\n- option 0 label: `Pass E2E`\n- option 0 description: `Selects the expected test outcome.`\n- option 1 label: `Fail E2E`\n- option 1 description: `Selects the alternate test outcome.`\nThe safe harness must dynamically detect that new pending question and submit option index 0 exactly once. This avoids any free-text body and exercises the simplest proven picker byte contract.\n\n3. Safe output contract: only `{phase,httpStatus,questionId,questionCount,answerable,requestId,outcome,coverageEpoch,status}`; no question text/header/descriptions/option labels/fingerprint, decrypted bodies, JWT, key refs, device IDs, nonces, terminal snapshots, or transcript content. It may log opaque IDs needed for DB correlation, but avoid dumping complete envelopes/bodies.\n\n4. DB proof command concept (run read-only through a small `bun:sqlite`/existing DB utility; output selected columns only): query `answer_attempts WHERE request_id=?`, require confirmed + resolved timestamp + lease, null failure, `guards_passed_json='[]'`. Re-run the status read with the same requestId/coverageEpoch—never resend `/v1/answer`.\n\nDo NOT use unchanged `closed_loop.py`, `closed_loop3.py`, or `emu.ts --quiet`; all still persist or print decrypted question/tree data. I did not execute or edit anything.\n</agent-message>"}
