{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-12T02:34:11.337Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a03883048daf6c57d</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>call_Ec7eLwRo4vQsHhvKuljAUl2P</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\083b7de7-951b-4059-a4aa-3dd81cb5a6cf\\tasks\\a03883048daf6c57d.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Diagnose phone free-text failure\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Investigated the physical phone free-text failure using non-sensitive metadata only.\n\n- The phone’s free-text request reached the desktop.\n- It was durably recorded as `confirmed`.\n- PTY settlement completed 5 ms after intake.\n- `failure_code` was null.\n- Guard evidence was empty (`[]`), as required by the guardless path.\n- The pending question was retracted after settlement.\n- No answer refusal or bridge error occurred for that request.\n- The later emulator single-select test used a separate request/question 56 seconds later and did not interfere with the free-text write.\n\nOne genuine test-harness issue was found: the emulator reused the physical phone’s paired device identity and temporarily negotiated fewer capabilities. This caused the phone’s subsequent FCM registration to receive `capability_unsupported` until the real phone performed a full-capability re-hello. That happened after the free-text answer had already confirmed, but emulator testing must use a distinct paired identity to avoid disturbing the phone session.\n\nTherefore, the reported free-text problem is downstream of the confirmed desktop write—most likely phone result rendering/state—not an answer-path or screen-off barrier.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>0</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>9</tool_uses><duration_ms>104706</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
