{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-12T02:36:40.382Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<agent-message from=\"emulator-identity\">\nTask: distinct paired emulator identity without touching physical devices. NOT created: production `openPairing()` currently logs the entire secret-bearing QR URI at `packages/host-service/src/companion/index.ts:1246-1249` (`{ qrUri: handle.qrUri, ... }`), directly violating the no-secret-logging rule documented in `pairing.ts:220-225`. Calling authenticated local tRPC `companion.openPairing` would therefore persist the 120-second pairing code in host-service.log. Manual DB/key insertion would bypass the real pairing boundary and is not acceptable. Safe next step: production fix that log to `{ pairingRef: handle.pairingRef, expiresAtMs }`, run required simplify/review/build/install workflow, then pair a fresh emulator device through authenticated local tRPC + real `/pair/kex` and `/pair/confirm`; store only the client-side derived key in protected scratch and use its new deviceId in E2E. Until then, do not run `safe-e2e.ts`/`safe-freetext-e2e.ts` because they reuse the physical phone identity and perturb its capability session. No existing device state was changed.\n</agent-message>"}
