{"parentUuid":"981fecfb-c26d-4206-8dd1-aa0621ba3859","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"resp_01043f6cd43141cb016a7c587d76e081919072c64734b7b0c7","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"codex-gpt-5-6-sol","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":660,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":165376,"output_tokens":36,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_ctDIpwGlkhVdh8EMVtTy4R3N","name":"TaskOutput","input":{"task_id":"ab7440d879a41441f","block":true,"timeout":300000}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_details":null},"attributionSkill":"windows-computer-use","type":"assistant","uuid":"b69fb6f6-79d2-45d6-b4c7-a5c90b7aa1c3","timestamp":"2026-08-12T11:26:57.339Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\installed-asar-check","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.228","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-12T11:31:34.975Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<agent-message from=\"settlement-design\">\nTask: design honest settlement without restoring any answer barrier.\n\nRecommended minimal architecture: split PTY delivery from AskUserQuestion settlement.\n\n1. Add durable status `accepted` between `in_flight` and `confirmed`.\n- `accepted` means every protocol-v3 frame got daemon `input-ok`, then the ledger outcome was durably written/read back.\n- `confirmed` additionally requires positive evidence that the exact captured tool call ended: matching PostToolUse `companionQuestionResolved` (`hostTerminalId` + `toolUseId`), or matching transcript `tool_result` as a positive fallback.\n- Missing/unreadable transcript, missing hook, renderer/display/lock state, binding, liveness, etc. NEVER vetoes, refuses, or downgrades the write. It simply leaves a terminal `accepted` delivery awaiting settlement. Protocol-v2 remains `unconfirmed`.\n\n2. Do not resolve/remove the question at PTY ack.\n- Remove `deps.questions.resolve(...)` from `answer.ts:1083-1109`.\n- Leave the question pending/discoverable in tree/question/heartbeat after `accepted`.\n- Resolve/retract only after the exact tool-use settlement is observed and the ledger has durably upgraded `accepted -> confirmed` and read it back.\n- This directly fixes the incident shape: wrong/stale PTY may accept bytes, but no matching PostToolUse/tool_result arrives, so the UI never lies or removes the still-open question.\n\n3. Use the existing strongest signals, not screen parsing.\n- Hook already emits exact completion at `apps/desktop/.../pane-map-hook.ts:2144-2157`; sink verifies matching host terminal/toolUse at `question-store.ts:1860-1889`.\n- Transcript fallback already positively matches `tool_result.tool_use_id` at `question-store.ts:1271-1313`.\n- Screen snapshots, PTY output-change, daemon drain, and renderer state are not settlement proof and must remain uninvolved.\n\n4. Make the hook/write race durable.\n- PostToolUse can arrive before answer.ts records `accepted`. Add a durable `settlement_observed_at_ms` (or a small `answer_settlements` row keyed by question/tool-use) rather than relying on memory.\n- Hook transaction records the positive observation. If row is already accepted, upgrade to confirmed. If still in_flight, leave observation; answer’s post-ack transaction sees it and writes confirmed rather than accepted. Never confirm before all frames ack.\n- Add a durable per-question active-delivery fence so a second requestId cannot resend while an accepted answer awaits settlement; clients poll, never auto-retry.\n\n5. Wire a settlement coordinator in `companion/index.ts`.\n- Both notifying hook sink and transcript reconcile/status-poll fallback call one coordinator: record observation -> promote/readback ledger -> then `QuestionStore.resolve` -> publish/retract.\n- Desk answer with no remote attempt still resolves normally.\n- Change `question-store.reconcile` to report positive candidates rather than settling internally, or give it a callback that performs the ordered coordinator path.\n\n6. Wire/protocol semantics.\n- `AnswerResponse.status`: `accepted | confirmed | unconfirmed`; `AnswerStatusOutcome.known.status` likewise.\n- Phone/watch render accepted as “Delivered to terminal; waiting for Claude” and do not retry. Only confirmed says answered.\n- This is not a post-write downgrade: accepted is a separate, positive delivery state. It preserves PTY honesty while avoiding the current false semantic confirmation.\n\nConcrete files: `packages/host-service/src/db/schema.ts` (+ generated migration, never hand-edit), `companion/attempt-ledger.ts`, `types.ts`, `http.ts`, `answer.ts`, `question-store.ts`, `index.ts`, `PROTOCOL.md`, `FEATURES.md`; coordinated Android/Wear response/status parsing and UX. Hook script likely needs no payload change.\n\nRequired tests: ack-only => accepted + question pending; hook before/after ack race => confirmed only after both; wrong-PTY input-ok/no hook => accepted forever + discoverable; unreadable transcript unchanged; matching tool_result upgrades; mismatched terminal/toolUse cannot settle; restart preserves accepted; duplicate new request fenced; protocol-v2 unconfirmed; audit failures non-vetoing; E2E requires actual AskUser tool completion, never ledger alone; locked/renderer-off flow uses hook/tool-result and no screen reads.\n</agent-message>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-12T11:31:48.413Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>af606c3b01d24f2f6</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\083b7de7-951b-4059-a4aa-3dd81cb5a6cf\\tasks\\af606c3b01d24f2f6.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Design honest settlement\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Task: design honest answer settlement without restoring any answer barrier.\n\nRecommended design sent to the parent: add a durable two-phase `accepted → confirmed` lifecycle.\n\n- **`accepted`**: all protocol-v3 PTY frames acknowledged and outcome durably persisted/read back.\n- **`confirmed`**: the exact AskUserQuestion subsequently produced matching positive completion evidence—PostToolUse or transcript `tool_result`.\n- Never remove the pending question at PTY acknowledgment.\n- Missing/unreadable transcript, renderer, display, lock state, binding, liveness, markers, or capabilities never block or downgrade the write.\n- Record completion observations durably to handle hook-before-ledger races.\n- Fence duplicate requests while an accepted delivery awaits settlement.\n- Keep protocol-v2 `unconfirmed`.\n- Update phone/watch to show `accepted` as “Delivered to terminal; waiting for Claude,” never as answered.\n- Require E2E verification against actual AskUser completion, not ledger status alone.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>0</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>29</tool_uses><duration_ms>586058</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
