{"parentUuid":"60bee4d1-82b1-43f3-8fef-2507ad82dd5b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"queued_command","prompt":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ab7440d879a41441f</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>call_WF6HhvO1Li8G6vUxaqUVrfWB</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\083b7de7-951b-4059-a4aa-3dd81cb5a6cf\\tasks\\ab7440d879a41441f.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Trace stale PTY targeting\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Traced the incident’s captured question through host.db, the PTY daemon, and Claude’s transcript metadata.\n\n- **Wrong/stale PTY targeting is refuted for this incident.**\n  - The audited opaque terminal handle resolves to host terminal `f689…`.\n  - That terminal was bound to the same Claude session and workspace that emitted the question.\n  - The question ID cryptographically matches the corresponding AskUser tool call in that session.\n- The phone answer arrived at `02:27:05.718Z`; the matching AskUser `tool_result` appeared at `02:27:06.059Z`—**341 ms later**. The intended Claude picker consumed the answer.\n- The visible question remaining on screen was therefore a **stale renderer terminal frame/repaint**, not failed delivery.\n- The bridge currently settles and retracts the question immediately after PTY acknowledgment at `packages/host-service/src/companion/answer.ts:1083`, roughly 5 ms after intake—before semantic settlement appears.\n- Safest fix without reintroducing barriers:\n  1. Keep `confirmed` semantics unchanged: daemon acknowledgment plus durable ledger write/readback.\n  2. Do not settle/retract `QuestionStore` merely on PTY acknowledgment.\n  3. Let positive PostToolUse/transcript evidence settle it through `packages/host-service/src/companion/question-store.ts:1960`.\n  4. Trigger a best-effort, non-vetoing repaint nudge after confirmed input using the existing mechanism at `packages/host-service/src/terminal/terminal.ts:1374`.\n  5. Never downgrade or refuse an answer if repaint or transcript observation fails.\n- No general cross-terminal mapping defect was found: capture, final arbitration, adoption, and writes retain the same host terminal/workspace identity.\n- `packages/host-service/src/trpc/router/notifications/notifications.ts:160` also contains stale documentation claiming retired guards still secure forged captures.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>0</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>52</tool_uses><duration_ms>760434</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","commandMode":"task-notification","timestamp":"2026-08-12T11:34:19.174Z"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b66df76e-3916-4ce8-9642-f1476e32d464","timestamp":"2026-08-12T11:34:19.174Z","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\installed-asar-check","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.228","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
