{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-12T12:50:55.850Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>abf8f40cae1ab9b59</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>call_NHYFrDrZiPjouoVSNSrhRTir</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\083b7de7-951b-4059-a4aa-3dd81cb5a6cf\\tasks\\abf8f40cae1ab9b59.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Review implementation altitude\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Corrected ALTITUDE review completed against the requested unified diff and sent to `implement-fixes`.\n\nOne finding: question-level durable ownership should be arbitrated atomically inside `claimForAnswer()`, rather than split between the claim and a later `findQuestionFence()` lookup.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>0</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>8</tool_uses><duration_ms>75159</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-12T12:51:05.612Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>af90fa5a91b586b93</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\083b7de7-951b-4059-a4aa-3dd81cb5a6cf\\tasks\\af90fa5a91b586b93.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Simplify review efficiency\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## Efficiency review — uncommitted working-tree diff\n\nTarget: 8 modified files in the shared checkout (`nudgeRepaint` + `markRemoteAnswered` + `findQuestionFence` batch). My worktree was clean; the diff lives in `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64` and I reconstructed it by normalized directory diff (git ops there are blocked for me). No changes outside `packages/host-service/src` (`routeTree.gen.ts`, `file-icons` are generated/untracked).\n\n### 1. Unindexed full-table scan per answer, inside the terminal lock — HIGH\n`C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\attempt-ledger.ts:744`\n`findQuestionFence` filters `answer_attempts` by `question_id`, but that column has no index — `packages\\host-service\\src\\db\\schema.ts:417` declares only `answer_attempts_created_at_ms_idx`; PK is `request_id`. Table is never pruned by design (`schema.ts:439-441`, LEDGER-KEEP-ATTEMPTS), so the scan is O(every answer attempt ever made on this host) and grows for the install's life. Driver is better-sqlite3 → synchronous → blocks the host-service event loop, and the call site (`companion\\answer.ts:779`, reached from `answer.ts:1098`) is **inside `locks.runExclusive`**, so it also lengthens the per-terminal critical section. `.all()` materializes and deserializes every matching row to use exactly one.\nCheaper: `index(\"answer_attempts_question_id_idx\").on(table.questionId)` + `.limit(1)` / `.get()` → one index seek, one row. (Index needs a drizzle migration — I did not generate one.)\nBonus: `schema.ts:416` comment \"nothing else queries by anything but the key\" is now false and should move with the index.\n\n### 2. Redraw latency queued behind a serialized fs append — MEDIUM\n`packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer.ts:1145-1172`\nConfirmed path order is `recordOutcome` → `await appendAnswerAudit` → `markRemoteAnswered` → `nudgeRepaint`. `audit.append` (`companion\\audit.ts:56-70,111-114`) is a *serialized* chain that does `open(a) + write + close` per line, so every confirmed answer pays one fs round trip — plus queueing behind any in-flight append — before the terminal is told to redraw. Nothing in the repaint or the provenance mark depends on the audit line; the stated ordering constraint is only \"after the durable confirmed row exists\", which `recordOutcome` already satisfies.\nCheaper: hoist `markRemoteAnswered` + `nudgeRepaint` above the audit append (audit stays best-effort, non-vetoing) → user-visible redraw no longer waits on disk.\n\n### 3. Diff extends pending-record lifetime → recurring 8 MiB transcript scans — MEDIUM\n`packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\question-store.ts:1964` (`markRemoteAnswered`) + `:2009-2114` (`reconcile`)\nThe new design deliberately leaves a durably-confirmed answer `pending` until the exact PostToolUse arrives. Every such record stays in `listPending()` and is therefore re-visited by each reconcile pass: `stat` + potential full scan (`TOOL_RESULT_SCAN_BYTES = 8_388_608`, `question-store.ts:158`) with JSONL parse. `unreadable` verdicts are deliberately not cached (`:2039`), so a question whose `tool_use` has scrolled out of the 8 MiB tail (long session), or whose hook died — the documented ARM64 failure mode — pays a full 8 MiB read + parse **every pass, per question, forever** (until the 24 h prune). The loop is also `await`-sequential (`:2020`), so N pending questions serialize.\nCheaper: (a) split `unreadable`-from-fs-error (transient, don't cache) from `unreadable`-because-`sawToolUse`-missed (`question-store.ts:1306`) — the latter is a pure function of identical bytes and is safe to cache under the same stat mark; (b) `Promise.all` / bounded concurrency over pending questions instead of a serial await loop.\n\n### 4. Duplicate ledger writes + readbacks on the downgrade path — LOW\n`packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer.ts:1120-1134`, outer catch at `:1322`\n`recordOutcome` is write + readback (`attempt-ledger.ts:631-644`); the confirmed→unconfirmed downgrade calls it twice = 4 synchronous DB ops, and the outer catch issues a third `ledger.get`. Cheaper: have `recordOutcome` return the read-back record so the downgrade reuses it, and pass the known status to the outer catch instead of re-reading. Cold path only — cost is a few sync sqlite ops, not correctness.\n\n### 5. Test harness allocates the whole map per lookup — LOW (test-only)\n`packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer-guardless.test.ts` (`memoryLedger.findQuestionFence`)\n`[...records.values()].find(...)` copies the map on every call. `for (const record of records.values())` is the same semantics with no allocation.\n\n### Checked, no findings\n- **Long-lived closures / retained scopes:** the repaint `setTimeout` closure (`terminal.ts:1389`) retains only `session` for `REPAINT_NUDGE_RESTORE_MS` and is generation- and liveness-guarded. `nudgeTerminalSessionRepaint` (`terminal.ts:1400`) is a map lookup + call.\n- **Startup blocking:** `assertAnswerDeps`'s new `nudgeRepaint` check (`answer.ts:296`) is a `typeof` test; the old writer probe it sits beside was already removed. No new sync fs at startup.\n- **Hot-path regressions elsewhere:** `index.ts` change is wiring plus dropping `qrUri` from a log line (strictly less work); `question-store.resolve` change is two `??`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>172600</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>50</tool_uses><duration_ms>513390</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"remove","timestamp":"2026-08-12T12:51:08.660Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a8d5e3bb38fc80d24</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>call_rLdoDzT07ufaUbcfwvRbpOlz</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\083b7de7-951b-4059-a4aa-3dd81cb5a6cf\\tasks\\a8d5e3bb38fc80d24.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Review answer fence changes\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Review complete. Diff isolated (primary HEAD == worktree HEAD 25fcc9e93; compared trees directly, CRLF-noise filtered): `FEATURES.md` + 6 host-service production files + 2 test files.\n\n---\n\n[MAJOR] C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\index.ts:1948\nDefect: `nudgeRepaint: nudgeTerminalSessionRepaint` wires an impl that destructures `{terminalId, workspaceId}` (terminal.ts:1415-1420), but the only call site passes a `HostTerminalRef` — keys `hostTerminalId`/`hostWorkspaceId` (answer.ts:957-960, called at answer.ts:1164).\nFailure: Every confirmed companion answer calls `writableSession(undefined, undefined)` → `{error: \"Terminal session not found\"}` → repaint NEVER happens in production; only `companion.answer.repaint_failed` log lines. The entire repaint half of this diff is dead on arrival, and the FEATURES.md claim (\"a best-effort PTY resize nudge asks Claude to repaint its consumed picker\") ships false. Tests pass because `answerHarness` uses a fake repaint that accepts `HostTerminalRef` (answer-guardless.test.ts:229, expects `[HOST]` = `{hostTerminalId, hostWorkspaceId}`), never the real adapter. Also a TS2322 at index.ts:1948, which only the absent type gate hides.\nFix: Adapt at the wiring site: `nudgeRepaint: ({hostTerminalId, hostWorkspaceId}) =&gt; nudgeTerminalSessionRepaint({terminalId: hostTerminalId, workspaceId: hostWorkspaceId})`.\n\n[MAJOR] C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\attempt-ledger.ts:752 (+ answer.ts:779)\nDefect: The fence counts `in_flight` rows of OTHER live requests, but `claimForAnswer` (attempt-ledger.ts:648) claims `in_flight` keyed on requestId only, BEFORE the lease/lock — so a concurrent request's pre-write claim reads as \"already delivered\".\nFailure: Phone and watch answer the same question near-simultaneously (the exact first-answer-wins scenario). Both claim `in_flight` (answer.ts:845). B then sits in the `await writer.prepare(...)` daemon round-trip (answer.ts:969) holding an `in_flight` row the whole time. A wins the lease, enters the lock, and `findQuestionFence` at answer.ts:779 sees B's row → A is refused 409 \"an answer for this question was already delivered … it will not be typed again\" though ZERO keystrokes were written by anyone. If B's fence read then beats A's outer-catch flip to `failed` (answer.ts:1322), B is refused too: two devices, both told \"already delivered\", nothing typed, question still pending. This violates the stated requirement — a pre-write claim is neither a durable duplicate nor an ambiguous write. Note `in_flight` inclusion IS load-bearing for the post-injection/pre-`recordOutcome` window (recordOutcome runs outside the lock at answer.ts:1120), so it cannot simply be dropped.\nFix: Split the states: claim as `claimed`, promote to `in_flight` durably INSIDE the lock immediately before the first keystroke; fence on `in_flight`/`confirmed`/`unconfirmed` only. Crash pre-write leaves non-fencing `claimed`; crash mid-type still fences.\n\n[MAJOR] C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\attempt-ledger.ts:759\nDefect: `findQuestionFence` throws a plain `Error` on an unvalidatable candidate row; thrown inside the lock pre-write, it hits the non-SealedError catch (answer.ts:1290) which durably records THIS request as `unconfirmed` — a fence status — though nothing was written.\nFailure: One corrupt/foreign/schema-drifted row with a fence status on question Q (e.g., a newer build's row this build's `validate` rejects) → every fresh answer request for Q not only 500s but each mints a NEW never-pruned `unconfirmed` row claiming \"may have been typed\". Even after the corruption is repaired, Q stays permanently fenced by rows that provably wrote zero bytes — a durable false ambiguous-write fence, and a direct violation of the \"corrupt row costs one requestId its status\" containment rule in FEATURES.md.\nFix: Throw a `sealed(503, \"internal\", \"nothing was written …\")` (or convert to sealed before the lock callback returns) so the outer catch records `failed`, which is not in the fence set.\n\n[MINOR] C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\question-store.ts:1967 (called from answer.ts:1156)\nDefect: `markRemoteAnswered` throws on an unknown questionId, and it runs after two `await`s (recordOutcome, audit append) during which the record can leave the store.\nFailure: Question asked &gt;24 h ago (settledAt falls back to `askedAtMs`, question-store.ts:1613), companion answer confirmed, a racing capture supersedes it stale and a `prune()` deletes it before answer.ts:1156 runs → throw → device receives an internal error and an `unconfirmed` audit line for an answer that is durably `confirmed` (row itself is safe; `recordOutcome` no-ops on non-in_flight). Retry then correctly gets the 409 fence.\nFix: Make `markRemoteAnswered` return false on unknown ids (mirror `markStale`'s tolerance) or wrap the call in the same log-only handling as the repaint.\n\n[MINOR] C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer.ts:788-792\nDefect: The fence 409 hardcodes `outcome: \"answered\"` and message \"was already delivered\", but the fence row may be `unconfirmed` (partial/unknown write) or a live `in_flight`, and after a restart `resolvedBy` is null and `resolvedAtMs` null for non-confirmed rows.\nFailure: A phone polling after an `unconfirmed` whole-sequence failure sees a later fresh request answered with `outcome: \"answered\"` — overclaiming certainty the v2-daemon `unconfirmed` contract deliberately refuses elsewhere.\nFix: Derive the detail from `durableFence.status` (answered vs may-have-been-delivered) instead of a constant.\n\nChecked and clean: secret pairing log fix (QR URI removed from logs; `pairingRef` exists at pairing.ts:238 and is genuinely non-secret; FEATURES.md text updated with markers intact); notifications.ts (comment-only); PostToolUse-before-provenance race (handled bidirectionally — `resolve` inherits `remoteAnswerBy` at question-store.ts:1958-1959, `markRemoteAnswered` back-stamps a resolved record at 1974-1977, both orders tested); stale-picker settlement (confirmed answers stay pending until exact-toolUseId PostToolUse/transcript settlement; supersede path at question-store.ts:1852-1877 intact); fresh-request fence excludes `failed`/`closed_not_received` so clean failures stay answerable; crash-mid-type and crash-post-ack both leave a durable fence and post-restart the question is unknown (no retype path); `assertAnswerDeps` wired at the sole composition root (index.ts:814).\n\n**FIX-FIRST**</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>138969</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>57</tool_uses><duration_ms>814067</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"remove","timestamp":"2026-08-12T12:51:08.660Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a99be40210d8caf62</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\083b7de7-951b-4059-a4aa-3dd81cb5a6cf\\tasks\\a99be40210d8caf62.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Simplify review reuse\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Reviewed the uncommitted diff (9 files, companion answer path). Note: it lives in the **shared checkout** `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64`, not my worktree — my worktree is clean at the same sha, so I reconstructed the diff by EOL-normalized content comparison. Paths below are shared-checkout paths.\n\nReuse findings (quality only, no edits made):\n\n**1. MAJOR — raw SQL reimplements drizzle `ne()` / `inArray()`**\n`C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\attempt-ledger.ts:744-767`\nNew `findQuestionFence` hand-writes `` sql`${answerAttempts.requestId} &lt;&gt; ${excludeRequestId}` `` and `` sql`${answerAttempts.status} IN ('in_flight', 'confirmed', 'unconfirmed')` ``. House helpers exist and are used for exactly this shape elsewhere: `ne(...)` (terminal.ts:2285, persistence.ts:234) and `inArray(terminalSessions.status, [\"exited\",\"disposed\"])` (persistence.ts:377); this same file already uses `eq(answerAttempts.status, \"in_flight\")` at :381/:721.\nCost: status literals inside the SQL string are untyped — renaming or adding an `AnswerAttemptStatus` value type-checks clean and silently un-fences the double-type path, the single invariant this function exists to enforce.\n\n**2. MAJOR — hand-rolled `QuestionStore` fake copies the production logic under test**\n`...\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer-guardless.test.ts:201-226`\n`answerHarness` builds `{get, byHostTerminal, markRemoteAnswered, markStale} as unknown as QuestionStore`, and its `markRemoteAnswered` body is a line-for-line copy of the new production one (`question-store.ts:1964-1979`). The real factory `createQuestionStore(...)` is the existing helper, already used with in-memory fixtures by four sibling tests (question-lifecycle.test.ts:80, question-freshness.test.ts:80, push-retract.test.ts:118).\nCost: the \"keeps phone provenance when positive settlement wins the marking race\" test asserts the fake's behaviour, not the store's — change the real precedence rule and this test stays green. The cast also erases every unimplemented method, so a new `QuestionStore` member never surfaces here.\n\n**3. MEDIUM — fence status-set duplicated across prod SQL and test double**\n`...\\answer-guardless.test.ts:163-171` vs `...\\attempt-ledger.ts:752`\n`{in_flight, confirmed, unconfirmed}` is spelled out twice, in two languages. No named constant exists (searched: no `isFencingStatus` / status-set export).\nCost: two edits per status change, and drift is invisible — the test would keep passing against its own stale copy.\n\n**4. MEDIUM — `already_resolved` sealed envelope built twice, 25 lines apart**\n`...\\companion\\answer.ts:750-759` (pre-existing) and `:784-793` (new)\nBoth throw `sealed(409, \"already_resolved\", …, {resolvedBy, resolvedAtMs, outcome: \"answered\"})`. An `alreadyResolved(resolvedBy, resolvedAtMs, detail)` helper collapses them.\nCost: the wire payload shape for this code now has two authors; adding a field to the `already_resolved` contract requires finding both.\n\n**5. MEDIUM — remote-provenance precedence encoded in two places**\n`...\\question-store.ts:1958-1959` (`resolve`) and `:1974-1977` (`markRemoteAnswered`)\n\"Remote answer wins over the settling caller\" is implemented once as `?? ` fallbacks and once as an if-branch overwrite. Also, `markRemoteAnswered:1965-1970` is the third copy of the `byId.get` + throw-on-unknown preamble (`resolve:1947`, `markStale:1982`) — a `requireQuestion(questionId, op)` helper already has two callers waiting.\nCost: the race rule can be changed in one branch and not the other, producing an answer whose provenance depends on which path settled it.\n\n**6. LOW — second `AnswerDeps` builder in a file that already has one**\n`...\\answer-guardless.test.ts:177` (`answerHarness`) does not compose `stubDeps` at `:93`; its inline question fixture (`:190-199`) also duplicates `questionItem()` in question-lifecycle.test.ts:20.\nCost: a new required `AnswerDeps` member must be added to both builders before the suite compiles.\n\n**Not a finding (checked, clean reuse):** `nudgeTerminalSessionRepaint` (`...\\terminal\\terminal.ts:1415-1435`) correctly reuses the existing private `nudgeRepaint(session)` and `writableSession(...)`, matching the established exported-wrapper pattern (`writeInputToSession`, `writeAcknowledgedInputToSession`). Its `error instanceof Error ? error.message : …` ternary repeats a host-service-wide idiom (a shared `toErrorMessage` exists in `packages/workspace-fs/src/error-message.ts` but is used nowhere in host-service) — following local convention, not worth changing in this diff. `notifications.ts` and `FEATURES.md` changes are comment/doc only.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>114440</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>45</tool_uses><duration_ms>487976</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"remove","timestamp":"2026-08-12T12:51:08.660Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>af90fa5a91b586b93</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\083b7de7-951b-4059-a4aa-3dd81cb5a6cf\\tasks\\af90fa5a91b586b93.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Simplify review efficiency\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## Efficiency review — uncommitted working-tree diff\n\nTarget: 8 modified files in the shared checkout (`nudgeRepaint` + `markRemoteAnswered` + `findQuestionFence` batch). My worktree was clean; the diff lives in `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64` and I reconstructed it by normalized directory diff (git ops there are blocked for me). No changes outside `packages/host-service/src` (`routeTree.gen.ts`, `file-icons` are generated/untracked).\n\n### 1. Unindexed full-table scan per answer, inside the terminal lock — HIGH\n`C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\attempt-ledger.ts:744`\n`findQuestionFence` filters `answer_attempts` by `question_id`, but that column has no index — `packages\\host-service\\src\\db\\schema.ts:417` declares only `answer_attempts_created_at_ms_idx`; PK is `request_id`. Table is never pruned by design (`schema.ts:439-441`, LEDGER-KEEP-ATTEMPTS), so the scan is O(every answer attempt ever made on this host) and grows for the install's life. Driver is better-sqlite3 → synchronous → blocks the host-service event loop, and the call site (`companion\\answer.ts:779`, reached from `answer.ts:1098`) is **inside `locks.runExclusive`**, so it also lengthens the per-terminal critical section. `.all()` materializes and deserializes every matching row to use exactly one.\nCheaper: `index(\"answer_attempts_question_id_idx\").on(table.questionId)` + `.limit(1)` / `.get()` → one index seek, one row. (Index needs a drizzle migration — I did not generate one.)\nBonus: `schema.ts:416` comment \"nothing else queries by anything but the key\" is now false and should move with the index.\n\n### 2. Redraw latency queued behind a serialized fs append — MEDIUM\n`packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer.ts:1145-1172`\nConfirmed path order is `recordOutcome` → `await appendAnswerAudit` → `markRemoteAnswered` → `nudgeRepaint`. `audit.append` (`companion\\audit.ts:56-70,111-114`) is a *serialized* chain that does `open(a) + write + close` per line, so every confirmed answer pays one fs round trip — plus queueing behind any in-flight append — before the terminal is told to redraw. Nothing in the repaint or the provenance mark depends on the audit line; the stated ordering constraint is only \"after the durable confirmed row exists\", which `recordOutcome` already satisfies.\nCheaper: hoist `markRemoteAnswered` + `nudgeRepaint` above the audit append (audit stays best-effort, non-vetoing) → user-visible redraw no longer waits on disk.\n\n### 3. Diff extends pending-record lifetime → recurring 8 MiB transcript scans — MEDIUM\n`packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\question-store.ts:1964` (`markRemoteAnswered`) + `:2009-2114` (`reconcile`)\nThe new design deliberately leaves a durably-confirmed answer `pending` until the exact PostToolUse arrives. Every such record stays in `listPending()` and is therefore re-visited by each reconcile pass: `stat` + potential full scan (`TOOL_RESULT_SCAN_BYTES = 8_388_608`, `question-store.ts:158`) with JSONL parse. `unreadable` verdicts are deliberately not cached (`:2039`), so a question whose `tool_use` has scrolled out of the 8 MiB tail (long session), or whose hook died — the documented ARM64 failure mode — pays a full 8 MiB read + parse **every pass, per question, forever** (until the 24 h prune). The loop is also `await`-sequential (`:2020`), so N pending questions serialize.\nCheaper: (a) split `unreadable`-from-fs-error (transient, don't cache) from `unreadable`-because-`sawToolUse`-missed (`question-store.ts:1306`) — the latter is a pure function of identical bytes and is safe to cache under the same stat mark; (b) `Promise.all` / bounded concurrency over pending questions instead of a serial await loop.\n\n### 4. Duplicate ledger writes + readbacks on the downgrade path — LOW\n`packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer.ts:1120-1134`, outer catch at `:1322`\n`recordOutcome` is write + readback (`attempt-ledger.ts:631-644`); the confirmed→unconfirmed downgrade calls it twice = 4 synchronous DB ops, and the outer catch issues a third `ledger.get`. Cheaper: have `recordOutcome` return the read-back record so the downgrade reuses it, and pass the known status to the outer catch instead of re-reading. Cold path only — cost is a few sync sqlite ops, not correctness.\n\n### 5. Test harness allocates the whole map per lookup — LOW (test-only)\n`packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer-guardless.test.ts` (`memoryLedger.findQuestionFence`)\n`[...records.values()].find(...)` copies the map on every call. `for (const record of records.values())` is the same semantics with no allocation.\n\n### Checked, no findings\n- **Long-lived closures / retained scopes:** the repaint `setTimeout` closure (`terminal.ts:1389`) retains only `session` for `REPAINT_NUDGE_RESTORE_MS` and is generation- and liveness-guarded. `nudgeTerminalSessionRepaint` (`terminal.ts:1400`) is a map lookup + call.\n- **Startup blocking:** `assertAnswerDeps`'s new `nudgeRepaint` check (`answer.ts:296`) is a `typeof` test; the old writer probe it sits beside was already removed. No new sync fs at startup.\n- **Hot-path regressions elsewhere:** `index.ts` change is wiring plus dropping `qrUri` from a log line (strictly less work); `question-store.resolve` change is two `??`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>172600</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>50</tool_uses><duration_ms>513390</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
